1
00:00:00,041 --> 00:00:00,041
25.000

2
00:01:41,810 --> 00:01:43,520
There was me.

3
00:01:43,978 --> 00:01:46,690
That is, Alex,
and my three droogs.

4
00:01:46,940 --> 00:01:50,610
That is, Pete, Georgie and Dim.

5
00:01:50,985 --> 00:01:54,572
And we sat in the Korova Milk Bar,
trying to make up our rassoodocks...

6
00:01:54,823 --> 00:01:57,075
... what to do with the evening.

7
00:01:58,785 --> 00:02:01,871
The Korova Milk Bar sold milk plus.

8
00:02:02,122 --> 00:02:05,750
Milk plus vellocet or
synthemesc or drencrom...

9
00:02:06,001 --> 00:02:08,003
... which is what we were drinking.

10
00:02:08,545 --> 00:02:09,921
This would sharpen you up...

11
00:02:10,171 --> 00:02:14,092
...and make you ready for a bit
of the old ultra-violence.

12
00:02:18,471 --> 00:02:21,975
In Dublin's fair city

13
00:02:22,642 --> 00:02:26,771
Where the girls are so pretty

14
00:02:27,856 --> 00:02:30,900
I first set my eyes

15
00:02:31,985 --> 00:02:35,572
On sweet Molly Malone

16
00:02:36,698 --> 00:02:41,369
As she wheeled her wheelbarrow

17
00:02:41,619 --> 00:02:45,999
Through streets broad and narrow

18
00:02:46,249 --> 00:02:50,712
Crying, "Cockles and mussels... "

19
00:02:51,629 --> 00:02:53,715
One thing I could never stand...

20
00:02:53,965 --> 00:02:56,384
... was to see a filthy,
dirty old drunkie...

21
00:02:56,634 --> 00:02:59,304
...howling away at the
filthy songs of his fathers...

22
00:02:59,554 --> 00:03:01,890
...and going "blerp blerp"
in between...

23
00:03:02,140 --> 00:03:06,394
...as it might be a filthy old
orchestra in his stinking guts.

24
00:03:06,644 --> 00:03:10,231
I could never stand to see anyone
like that, whatever his age.

25
00:03:10,482 --> 00:03:13,651
But more especially when he
was real old, like this one was.

26
00:03:21,284 --> 00:03:25,330
Can you spare some cutter,
me brothers?

27
00:03:28,500 --> 00:03:33,588
Go on! Do me in, you bastard cowards!
I don't want to live anyway.

28
00:03:33,838 --> 00:03:36,675
Not in a stinking world
like this.

29
00:03:39,427 --> 00:03:42,597
And what's so stinking about it?

30
00:03:42,847 --> 00:03:47,102
It's a stinking world because
there's no law and order anymore!

31
00:03:47,352 --> 00:03:50,438
It stinks because it lets
the young get onto the old...

32
00:03:50,689 --> 00:03:52,732
...like you done!

33
00:03:52,982 --> 00:03:57,821
It's no world
for an old man any longer.

34
00:03:58,405 --> 00:04:01,825
What kind of a world is it
at all?

35
00:04:02,075 --> 00:04:03,952
Men on the moon.

36
00:04:04,202 --> 00:04:06,705
Men spinning around the earth.

37
00:04:06,955 --> 00:04:10,000
And there's not no
attention paid...

38
00:04:10,208 --> 00:04:13,753
...to earthly
law and order no more.

39
00:04:14,129 --> 00:04:16,715
Oh, dear land

40
00:04:17,090 --> 00:04:19,426
I fought for thee

41
00:04:54,669 --> 00:04:58,465
It was at the derelict casino
that we came across Billy-boy...

42
00:04:58,715 --> 00:05:00,759
...and his four droogs.

43
00:05:01,092 --> 00:05:03,511
They were about to perform
a little of the old...

44
00:05:03,762 --> 00:05:07,724
...in-out, in-out on a weepy
young devotchka they had there.

45
00:05:57,857 --> 00:06:00,735
Well, if it isn't fat, stinking...

46
00:06:00,985 --> 00:06:05,281
...billy goat
Billy-boy in poison.

47
00:06:06,116 --> 00:06:07,742
How are thou...

48
00:06:07,992 --> 00:06:11,788
...thou globby bottle of cheap,
stinking chip-oil?

49
00:06:13,540 --> 00:06:16,126
Come and get one in the yarbles...

50
00:06:16,376 --> 00:06:18,253
...if you have any yarbles...

51
00:06:18,503 --> 00:06:21,506
...you eunuch jelly, thou.

52
00:06:24,968 --> 00:06:26,636
Let's get them, boys!

53
00:07:24,694 --> 00:07:26,112
The police!

54
00:07:26,696 --> 00:07:28,365
Come on. Let's go!

55
00:07:49,302 --> 00:07:53,848
The Durango 95 purred away
real horrorshow.

56
00:07:54,099 --> 00:07:58,353
A nice, warm vibratey feeling
all through your guttiwuts.

57
00:07:58,603 --> 00:08:01,773
Soon it was trees and dark,
my brothers...

58
00:08:02,023 --> 00:08:04,567
... with real country dark.

59
00:08:41,438 --> 00:08:44,607
We fillied around with other
travelers of the night...

60
00:08:44,858 --> 00:08:47,193
...playing Hogs of the Road.

61
00:08:47,444 --> 00:08:49,446
Then we headed west.

62
00:08:49,696 --> 00:08:53,366
What we were after now
was the old surprise visit.

63
00:08:53,616 --> 00:08:54,868
That was a real kick...

64
00:08:55,118 --> 00:08:59,581
...and good for laughs and
lashing of the old ultra-violent.

65
00:09:48,004 --> 00:09:50,006
Who on earth could that be?

66
00:09:59,099 --> 00:10:00,684
I'll go and see.

67
00:10:11,444 --> 00:10:13,113
Yes, who is it?

68
00:10:13,321 --> 00:10:17,367
Excuse me, can you please help?
There's been a terrible accident!

69
00:10:18,451 --> 00:10:22,706
My friend's bleeding to death!
Can I please use your telephone?

70
00:10:22,956 --> 00:10:26,209
We don't have a telephone.
You'll have to go somewhere else.

71
00:10:26,459 --> 00:10:29,170
But, missus, it's a matter
of life and death!

72
00:10:29,421 --> 00:10:30,714
Who is it, dear?

73
00:10:30,964 --> 00:10:33,508
A young man.
He says there's been an accident.

74
00:10:33,758 --> 00:10:36,428
He wants to use the telephone.

75
00:10:37,429 --> 00:10:39,931
I suppose you better let him in.

76
00:10:40,932 --> 00:10:42,767
Wait a minute, will you?

77
00:10:44,936 --> 00:10:48,231
I'm sorry, but we don't usually
let strangers in...

78
00:11:00,326 --> 00:11:02,203
What do you want from me?

79
00:11:05,957 --> 00:11:08,710
Pete, check the rest
of the house. Dim...

80
00:11:13,590 --> 00:11:15,842
I'm singing in the rain

81
00:11:16,885 --> 00:11:18,803
Just singing in the rain

82
00:11:19,637 --> 00:11:21,431
What a glorious feeling

83
00:11:22,349 --> 00:11:23,850
I'm happy again

84
00:11:25,226 --> 00:11:27,062
I'm laughing at clouds

85
00:11:28,188 --> 00:11:29,564
So dark up above

86
00:11:30,982 --> 00:11:32,567
The sun's in my heart

87
00:11:33,985 --> 00:11:35,820
And I'm ready for love

88
00:11:37,447 --> 00:11:39,699
Let the stormy clouds chase

89
00:11:40,575 --> 00:11:42,494
Everyone from the place

90
00:11:44,871 --> 00:11:46,164
Come on with the rain

91
00:11:47,123 --> 00:11:49,250
I've a smile on my face

92
00:11:50,251 --> 00:11:52,295
I'll walk down the lane

93
00:11:53,296 --> 00:11:55,256
With a happy refrain

94
00:11:56,341 --> 00:11:58,218
And I'm singing

95
00:11:58,843 --> 00:12:00,303
Just singing...

96
00:12:02,472 --> 00:12:03,640
...in the rain

97
00:13:10,415 --> 00:13:11,875
Viddy well, little brother.

98
00:13:12,125 --> 00:13:13,793
Viddy well.

99
00:13:34,147 --> 00:13:37,984
We were all feeling a bit
shagged and fagged and fashed...

100
00:13:38,234 --> 00:13:42,822
...it having been an evening
of some small energy expenditure.

101
00:13:43,073 --> 00:13:48,036
So we got rid of the auto and
stopped at the Korova for a nightcap.

102
00:13:54,376 --> 00:13:55,835
Hello, Lucy.

103
00:13:56,961 --> 00:13:58,672
Had a busy night?

104
00:14:00,382 --> 00:14:02,759
We've been working hard too.

105
00:14:05,136 --> 00:14:06,971
Pardon me, Luce.

106
00:14:14,604 --> 00:14:18,191
There was some sophistos from
the TV studios around the corner...

107
00:14:18,441 --> 00:14:20,652
...laughing and govoreeting.

108
00:14:20,985 --> 00:14:26,116
The devotchka smeched away, not
caring about the wicked world one bit.

109
00:14:26,908 --> 00:14:30,286
Then the disk on the stereo
twanged off and out.

110
00:14:30,537 --> 00:14:33,832
And in the short silence
before the next one came on...

111
00:14:34,082 --> 00:14:37,252
...she suddenly came
with a burst of singing.

112
00:14:41,089 --> 00:14:43,425
And it was like, for a moment,
O my brothers...

113
00:14:43,675 --> 00:14:46,928
...some great bird
had flown into the milk bar.

114
00:14:47,178 --> 00:14:50,432
And I felt all the malenky
little hairs on my plott...

115
00:14:50,682 --> 00:14:52,559
...standing endwise.

116
00:14:52,934 --> 00:14:57,022
And the shivers crawling up
like slow, malenky lizards...

117
00:14:57,272 --> 00:14:58,898
...and then down again.

118
00:14:59,149 --> 00:15:01,860
Because I knew what she sang.

119
00:15:02,110 --> 00:15:05,530
It was a bit from
the glorious Ninth, by Ludwig van.

120
00:15:14,330 --> 00:15:16,458
What did you do that for?

121
00:15:16,708 --> 00:15:18,752
For being a bastard
with no manners.

122
00:15:19,002 --> 00:15:23,840
Without a dook of an idea about how
to comport yourself public-wise.

123
00:15:26,134 --> 00:15:28,928
I don't like you should
do what you done.

124
00:15:29,387 --> 00:15:32,807
And I'm not your brother no more
and wouldn't want to be.

125
00:15:36,269 --> 00:15:37,604
Watch that.

126
00:15:38,605 --> 00:15:43,735
Do watch that, if to continue
to be on live thou dost wish.

127
00:15:45,695 --> 00:15:46,946
Yarbles!

128
00:15:47,197 --> 00:15:49,949
Great, bouncy yarblockos to you!

129
00:15:50,367 --> 00:15:54,079
I'll meet you with chain
or nozh or britva anytime.

130
00:15:54,329 --> 00:15:56,998
I'm not having you aiming
tolchocks at me reasonless.

131
00:15:57,457 --> 00:16:00,335
It stands to reason,
I won't have it.

132
00:16:05,048 --> 00:16:08,468
A nozh scrap anytime you say.

133
00:16:23,358 --> 00:16:25,068
Doobidoob.

134
00:16:27,320 --> 00:16:29,280
A bit tired maybe.

135
00:16:31,366 --> 00:16:33,201
Best not to say more.

136
00:16:34,577 --> 00:16:37,038
Bedways is rightways now.

137
00:16:37,580 --> 00:16:40,709
So best we go homeways
and get a bit of spatchka.

138
00:16:41,001 --> 00:16:42,419
Right, right?

139
00:16:54,681 --> 00:16:57,392
Where I lived was with
my dada and mum...

140
00:16:57,642 --> 00:17:02,063
...in municipal flat block
18-A, Linear North.

141
00:18:27,857 --> 00:18:29,818
It had been a wonderful evening.

142
00:18:30,068 --> 00:18:33,613
And what I needed now
to give it the perfect ending...

143
00:18:33,863 --> 00:18:36,825
... was a bit
of the old Ludwig van.

144
00:19:26,916 --> 00:19:28,251
Oh, bliss!

145
00:19:28,835 --> 00:19:30,920
Bliss and heaven!

146
00:19:31,421 --> 00:19:36,009
It was gorgeousness and
gorgeosity made flesh.

147
00:19:36,801 --> 00:19:40,847
It was like a bird
of rarest spun heaven metal.

148
00:19:41,097 --> 00:19:44,559
Or like silvery wine
flowing in a spaceship...

149
00:19:44,809 --> 00:19:47,604
...gravity all nonsense now.

150
00:19:48,104 --> 00:19:49,564
As I slooshied...

151
00:19:49,814 --> 00:19:52,859
...I knew such lovely pictures.

152
00:20:12,337 --> 00:20:13,838
Alex. Alex!

153
00:20:21,054 --> 00:20:22,514
What do you want?

154
00:20:22,764 --> 00:20:24,307
It's past eight, Alex.

155
00:20:24,557 --> 00:20:27,644
You don't want to be
late for school, son.

156
00:20:29,104 --> 00:20:31,731
Bit of a pain in the gulliver, Mum.

157
00:20:31,981 --> 00:20:34,526
Leave us be,
and I'll try and sleep it off.

158
00:20:34,776 --> 00:20:37,529
And then I'll be as right
as dodgers for this after.

159
00:20:38,488 --> 00:20:41,574
But you've not been
to school all week, son.

160
00:20:41,825 --> 00:20:42,992
Got to rest, Mum.

161
00:20:43,576 --> 00:20:45,328
Got to get fit.

162
00:20:45,787 --> 00:20:49,290
Otherwise, I'm liable
to miss a lot more school.

163
00:20:49,541 --> 00:20:54,629
I'll put your breakfast in the oven.
I've got to be off meself now.

164
00:20:55,755 --> 00:20:59,926
All right, Mum.
Have a nice day at the factory.

165
00:21:04,264 --> 00:21:07,392
He's not feeling too good
again this morning, Dad.

166
00:21:07,642 --> 00:21:09,477
Yes. Yes, I heard.

167
00:21:09,978 --> 00:21:11,438
You know what time he got in?

168
00:21:11,730 --> 00:21:14,691
No, I don't.
I'd taken me sleepers.

169
00:21:17,360 --> 00:21:18,862
I wonder...

170
00:21:19,279 --> 00:21:23,324
...where exactly is it
he goes to work of evenings.

171
00:21:25,493 --> 00:21:26,911
Like he says...

172
00:21:27,162 --> 00:21:29,497
...it's mostly odd things he does.

173
00:21:29,748 --> 00:21:30,915
Helping-like...

174
00:21:31,166 --> 00:21:33,835
...here and there, as it might be.

175
00:22:15,460 --> 00:22:17,462
Hi, hi, hi, Mr. Deltoid.

176
00:22:17,712 --> 00:22:19,631
Funny surprise, seeing you here.

177
00:22:19,881 --> 00:22:23,802
Alex-boy!
Awake at last, yes?

178
00:22:24,427 --> 00:22:27,430
I met your mother
on the way to work, yes?

179
00:22:27,681 --> 00:22:29,724
She gave me the key.

180
00:22:32,519 --> 00:22:34,729
She said something about
a pain somewhere.

181
00:22:34,979 --> 00:22:37,941
Hence, not at school, yes?

182
00:22:38,274 --> 00:22:41,444
A rather intolerable pain
in the head, brother sir.

183
00:22:41,695 --> 00:22:43,822
It should be clear
by this afterlunch.

184
00:22:44,698 --> 00:22:47,283
Or certainly by this evening, yes.

185
00:22:47,534 --> 00:22:50,745
The evening's the great time,
isn't it, Alex-boy?

186
00:22:50,995 --> 00:22:54,541
-Cup of the old chai, sir?
-No time, no time.

187
00:22:54,791 --> 00:22:56,376
Sit, sit, sit!

188
00:22:57,961 --> 00:23:00,714
To what do I owe
this extreme pleasure, sir?

189
00:23:01,464 --> 00:23:02,632
Anything wrong, sir?

190
00:23:02,882 --> 00:23:06,720
Wrong? Why should you
think of anything being wrong?

191
00:23:06,970 --> 00:23:09,347
Have you been doing
something you shouldn't?

192
00:23:09,597 --> 00:23:10,890
Just a manner of speech.

193
00:23:11,141 --> 00:23:14,185
Yes, well, it's just a manner
of speech from your...

194
00:23:14,436 --> 00:23:17,689
...post-corrective advisor to you
that you watch out, little Alex.

195
00:23:17,939 --> 00:23:21,484
Because next time it's not
going to be the corrective school.

196
00:23:21,735 --> 00:23:26,031
Next time it'll be the Barley place,
and all my work ruined.

197
00:23:26,281 --> 00:23:28,074
If you've no respect
for yourself...

198
00:23:28,324 --> 00:23:31,411
...you at least might have some
for me, who sweated over you.

199
00:23:31,661 --> 00:23:35,749
A big, black mark, I tell you,
for every one we don't reclaim.

200
00:23:35,999 --> 00:23:39,210
A confession of failure
for every one of you...

201
00:23:39,461 --> 00:23:42,380
...who ends up in the stripy hole.

202
00:23:42,630 --> 00:23:44,466
I've been doing nothing I shouldn't.

203
00:23:44,716 --> 00:23:47,344
The millicents have nothing
on me, brother.

204
00:23:47,594 --> 00:23:48,887
Sir, I mean.

205
00:23:49,137 --> 00:23:51,681
Cut out this clever talk
about millicents.

206
00:23:51,931 --> 00:23:54,142
Just because the police
haven't picked you up...

207
00:23:54,392 --> 00:23:57,604
...doesn't mean that you've not
been up to some nastiness.

208
00:23:57,854 --> 00:24:02,984
There was a bit of nastiness last night.
Some very extreme nastiness, yes?

209
00:24:03,234 --> 00:24:07,405
A few of a certain Billy-boy's
friends were ambulanced off late.

210
00:24:07,655 --> 00:24:09,074
Your name was mentioned.

211
00:24:09,324 --> 00:24:11,534
The words got to me
by the usual channels.

212
00:24:11,785 --> 00:24:14,621
Certain friends of yours
were named also.

213
00:24:14,871 --> 00:24:18,083
Nobody can prove anything
about anybody, as usual.

214
00:24:18,333 --> 00:24:19,918
I'm warning you, little Alex...

215
00:24:20,168 --> 00:24:22,420
...being a good friend
to you as always...

216
00:24:22,671 --> 00:24:25,423
...the one man in this
sore and sick community...

217
00:24:25,674 --> 00:24:28,385
...who wants to save you
from yourself!

218
00:24:47,779 --> 00:24:49,489
What gets into you all?

219
00:24:49,739 --> 00:24:53,034
We've been studying the problem
for damn well near a century.

220
00:24:53,284 --> 00:24:55,412
But we get no farther
with our studies.

221
00:24:55,662 --> 00:24:58,164
You got a good home here.
Good, loving parents.

222
00:24:58,415 --> 00:25:00,542
You've got not too bad of a brain.

223
00:25:00,792 --> 00:25:03,962
Is it some devil
that crawls inside of you?

224
00:25:04,212 --> 00:25:06,089
Nobody's got anything on me.

225
00:25:06,339 --> 00:25:09,092
I been out of the millicents'
rookers for a long time.

226
00:25:09,342 --> 00:25:13,847
That's just what worries me.
A bit too long to be safe.

227
00:25:14,097 --> 00:25:15,932
You're about due, by my reckoning.

228
00:25:16,182 --> 00:25:17,475
That's why I'm warning you...

229
00:25:17,726 --> 00:25:21,229
...to keep your handsome
young proboscis out of the dirt.

230
00:25:21,479 --> 00:25:22,814
Do I make myself clear?

231
00:25:23,064 --> 00:25:24,482
As an unmuddied lake, sir.

232
00:25:24,733 --> 00:25:28,111
As clear as an azure sky
of deepest summer.

233
00:25:28,361 --> 00:25:30,655
You can rely on me, sir.

234
00:26:36,805 --> 00:26:38,390
Excuse me, brother.

235
00:26:38,640 --> 00:26:42,268
I ordered this two weeks ago.
Can you see if it's arrived?

236
00:26:43,645 --> 00:26:44,938
Just a minute.

237
00:27:11,214 --> 00:27:12,882
Pardon me, ladies.

238
00:27:21,474 --> 00:27:24,102
Enjoying that, are you, my darling?

239
00:27:26,688 --> 00:27:30,025
A bit cold and pointless,
isn't it, my lovely?

240
00:27:34,362 --> 00:27:37,282
What's happened to yours,
my little sister?

241
00:27:39,451 --> 00:27:40,910
Who you getting, bratty?

242
00:27:41,161 --> 00:27:43,288
Goggly Gogol?
Johnny Zhivago?

243
00:27:43,538 --> 00:27:45,415
The Heaven 17?

244
00:27:49,711 --> 00:27:53,548
What you got back home
to play your fuzzy warbles on?

245
00:27:53,798 --> 00:27:58,053
I bet you've got little
pitiful, portable picnic players.

246
00:27:58,303 --> 00:28:00,472
Come with Uncle
and hear all proper.

247
00:28:00,722 --> 00:28:03,767
Hear angel trumpets
and devil trombones.

248
00:28:04,017 --> 00:28:06,061
You are invited.

249
00:29:28,435 --> 00:29:29,394
Hi, hi, hi, there.

250
00:29:29,644 --> 00:29:30,645
Well, hello.

251
00:29:30,895 --> 00:29:33,523
He are here!
He have arrived!

252
00:29:33,773 --> 00:29:35,358
Hooray!

253
00:29:36,026 --> 00:29:38,820
Welly, welly, welly,
welly, welly, welly, well!

254
00:29:40,488 --> 00:29:45,243
To what do I owe the extreme pleasure
of this surprising visit?

255
00:29:50,582 --> 00:29:52,292
We got worried.

256
00:29:55,170 --> 00:30:00,050
There we were, waiting and drinking
away at the old knifey moloko...

257
00:30:00,759 --> 00:30:02,844
...and you had not turned up.

258
00:30:03,261 --> 00:30:05,472
And we thought
you might have been, like...

259
00:30:05,722 --> 00:30:08,058
...offended by something
or other.

260
00:30:08,308 --> 00:30:10,685
So around we come to your abode.

261
00:30:16,107 --> 00:30:18,318
Appy polly loggies.

262
00:30:18,610 --> 00:30:21,738
I had something of a pain
in the gulliver, so I had to sleep.

263
00:30:21,988 --> 00:30:24,824
I was not awakened
when I gave orders for wakening.

264
00:30:25,075 --> 00:30:27,494
Sorry about the pain.

265
00:30:28,203 --> 00:30:30,705
Using the gulliver
too much-like, maybe.

266
00:30:33,917 --> 00:30:37,379
Giving orders and
discipline and such, perhaps.

267
00:30:37,837 --> 00:30:40,173
You sure the pain is gone?

268
00:30:40,632 --> 00:30:43,718
You sure you'd not
be happier back in bed?

269
00:31:05,198 --> 00:31:09,494
Let's get things nice
and sparkling clear.

270
00:31:12,872 --> 00:31:15,333
This sarcasm,
if I may call it such...

271
00:31:15,583 --> 00:31:18,336
...does not become you,
my little brothers.

272
00:31:18,878 --> 00:31:23,299
As I am your droog and leader
I'm entitled to know what goes on.

273
00:31:25,176 --> 00:31:26,386
Now then, Dim.

274
00:31:26,636 --> 00:31:30,807
What does that great big
horsey gape of a grin portend?

275
00:31:32,809 --> 00:31:36,563
All right, no more
picking on Dim, brother.

276
00:31:36,813 --> 00:31:39,232
That's part of the new way.

277
00:31:47,032 --> 00:31:50,952
New way?
What's this about a new way?

278
00:31:52,245 --> 00:31:57,167
There's been some very large talk
behind my sleeping back, I know it.

279
00:31:58,543 --> 00:32:01,463
If you must have it,
have it, then.

280
00:32:02,213 --> 00:32:04,883
We go around shop crasting
and the like...

281
00:32:05,133 --> 00:32:08,720
...coming out with a pitiful
rookerfull of money each.

282
00:32:09,054 --> 00:32:11,306
And Will the English
in the coffee mesto...

283
00:32:11,556 --> 00:32:15,185
...saying he can fence anything
any malchick tries to crast.

284
00:32:15,435 --> 00:32:17,354
The shiny stuff. The ice!

285
00:32:17,604 --> 00:32:21,649
The big, big money's available,
is what Will the English says.

286
00:32:23,693 --> 00:32:26,988
And what will you do
with the big, big, big money?

287
00:32:27,238 --> 00:32:29,157
Have you not everything you need?

288
00:32:29,407 --> 00:32:32,327
If you need a motorcar,
you pluck it from the trees.

289
00:32:32,577 --> 00:32:35,622
If you need pretty polly,
you take it.

290
00:32:35,872 --> 00:32:40,460
Brother, you think and talk
sometimes like a little child.

291
00:32:41,336 --> 00:32:43,880
Tonight we pull a man-size crast.

292
00:32:45,799 --> 00:32:48,134
Good! Real horrorshow!

293
00:32:48,385 --> 00:32:50,762
Initiative comes
to thems that wait.

294
00:32:51,429 --> 00:32:54,432
I've taught you much,
my little droogies.

295
00:32:55,850 --> 00:32:59,229
Now tell me what you had in mind,
Georgie-boy.

296
00:33:02,565 --> 00:33:05,777
The old moloko plus first.
Would you not say?

297
00:33:06,027 --> 00:33:09,823
-Something to sharpen us up.
-Some moloko plus.

298
00:33:11,366 --> 00:33:16,162
You got to go there first.
We got a start on you. Moloko Plus!

299
00:33:24,087 --> 00:33:26,548
As we walked along
the flatblock marina...

300
00:33:26,798 --> 00:33:31,052
...I was calm on the outside,
but thinking all the time.

301
00:33:31,302 --> 00:33:33,847
So now it was to be
Georgie the General...

302
00:33:34,097 --> 00:33:36,558
...saying what we should do
and what not to do.

303
00:33:36,808 --> 00:33:40,729
And Dim as his mindless,
grinning bulldog.

304
00:33:40,979 --> 00:33:44,649
But suddenly I viddied that
thinking was for the gloopy ones...

305
00:33:44,899 --> 00:33:50,030
...and that the oomny ones used, like,
inspiration and what Bog sends.

306
00:33:50,530 --> 00:33:54,367
For now it was lovely music
that came to my aid.

307
00:33:54,617 --> 00:33:57,704
There was a window open
with a stereo on...

308
00:33:57,954 --> 00:34:01,249
...and I viddied right at once
what to do.

309
00:35:06,773 --> 00:35:10,360
I had not cut into any
of Dim's main cables.

310
00:35:10,610 --> 00:35:12,862
And so with the help
of a clean tashtook...

311
00:35:13,113 --> 00:35:15,490
...the red, red kroovy
soon stopped.

312
00:35:15,740 --> 00:35:19,411
And it did not take long to
quieten the two wounded soldiers...

313
00:35:19,661 --> 00:35:22,330
...down in the snug
of the Duke of New York.

314
00:35:23,248 --> 00:35:26,793
Now they knew who was
master and leader.

315
00:35:27,293 --> 00:35:29,212
Sheep, thought I.

316
00:35:29,462 --> 00:35:31,631
But a real leader knows
always when, like...

317
00:35:31,881 --> 00:35:35,135
...to give and show generous
to his unders.

318
00:35:37,721 --> 00:35:39,973
Now we're back to where we were.

319
00:35:40,223 --> 00:35:41,558
Yes?

320
00:35:42,392 --> 00:35:44,686
Just like before,
and all forgotten?

321
00:35:44,936 --> 00:35:46,563
Right, right, right?

322
00:35:48,314 --> 00:35:49,441
Right.

323
00:35:52,360 --> 00:35:53,445
Right.

324
00:35:56,906 --> 00:35:57,949
Right.

325
00:36:00,869 --> 00:36:03,038
Well, Georgie-boy...

326
00:36:03,413 --> 00:36:07,292
...this idea of yours for tonight.
Tell us all about it, then.

327
00:36:08,960 --> 00:36:10,045
Not tonight.

328
00:36:10,295 --> 00:36:11,963
Not this nochy.

329
00:36:12,589 --> 00:36:15,175
Come, come, come, Georgie-boy.

330
00:36:15,717 --> 00:36:19,054
You're a big, strong chelloveck,
like us all.

331
00:36:19,304 --> 00:36:22,599
We're not little children,
are we, Georgie-boy?

332
00:36:23,266 --> 00:36:26,895
What, then, didst thou
in thy mind have?

333
00:36:33,777 --> 00:36:35,653
It's this health farm.

334
00:36:36,780 --> 00:36:38,782
A bit out of the town.

335
00:36:39,783 --> 00:36:41,284
Isolated.

336
00:36:42,369 --> 00:36:46,998
It's owned by this rich ptitsa
who lives there with her cats.

337
00:36:47,624 --> 00:36:52,128
The place is shut down for a week
and she's completely on her own.

338
00:36:53,463 --> 00:36:57,175
It's full up with, like,
gold and silver...

339
00:36:57,425 --> 00:36:59,427
...and, like, jewels.

340
00:37:00,887 --> 00:37:04,766
Tell me more, Georgie-boy.
Tell me more.

341
00:37:10,438 --> 00:37:11,773
Oh, shit!

342
00:37:30,625 --> 00:37:31,459
Who's there?

343
00:37:32,043 --> 00:37:34,045
Excuse me, can you please help?

344
00:37:34,295 --> 00:37:35,797
There's been a terrible accident!

345
00:37:36,047 --> 00:37:38,967
Can I please use your telephone
for an ambulance?

346
00:37:40,051 --> 00:37:42,012
I'm frightfully sorry.

347
00:37:42,887 --> 00:37:46,474
There's a telephone in the
public house a mile down the road.

348
00:37:46,725 --> 00:37:48,518
I suggest you use that.

349
00:37:48,768 --> 00:37:50,812
But missus, this is an emergency!

350
00:37:51,062 --> 00:37:52,856
It's a matter of life and death!

351
00:37:53,106 --> 00:37:56,901
Me friend's lying in the middle
of the road, bleeding to death!

352
00:37:57,819 --> 00:38:02,866
I'm very sorry, but I never open
the door to strangers after dark.

353
00:38:05,201 --> 00:38:06,995
Very well, madam.

354
00:38:07,412 --> 00:38:09,622
You can't be blamed
for being suspicious...

355
00:38:09,873 --> 00:38:13,668
...with so many scoundrels
and rogues of the night about.

356
00:38:13,918 --> 00:38:16,463
I'll try and get help
at the pub, then.

357
00:38:16,713 --> 00:38:19,174
I'm sorry if I disturbed you.

358
00:38:19,424 --> 00:38:22,510
Thank you very much.
Good night.

359
00:38:59,089 --> 00:39:00,548
Dim, bend down.

360
00:39:02,884 --> 00:39:05,804
I'll get in that window
and open the front door.

361
00:39:34,416 --> 00:39:36,209
Radlett Police Station?

362
00:39:36,459 --> 00:39:40,380
Good evening. It's Miss Weathers
at Woodmere Health Farm.

363
00:39:42,382 --> 00:39:46,344
I'm sorry to bother you, but
something rather odd just happened.

364
00:39:46,594 --> 00:39:49,431
It's probably nothing at all,
but you never know.

365
00:39:50,348 --> 00:39:53,727
A young man rang the bell,
asking to use the telephone.

366
00:39:53,977 --> 00:39:56,229
He said there's been
some kind of accident.

367
00:39:56,479 --> 00:39:58,940
The thing that caught my
attention was what he said.

368
00:39:59,190 --> 00:40:03,069
His words sounded like those quoted
in the papers this morning...

369
00:40:03,319 --> 00:40:07,532
...in connection with the writer
and his wife who were assaulted.

370
00:40:08,825 --> 00:40:10,869
Just a few minutes ago.

371
00:40:13,121 --> 00:40:14,914
If you think that's necessary.

372
00:40:15,165 --> 00:40:17,876
But I'm quite sure
he's gone away now.

373
00:40:19,502 --> 00:40:21,212
All right, fine.

374
00:40:22,172 --> 00:40:24,299
Thank you very much.

375
00:40:28,845 --> 00:40:30,472
Hi, hi, hi, there.

376
00:40:30,722 --> 00:40:32,057
At last we meet.

377
00:40:32,307 --> 00:40:36,978
Our brief govorett through the
letter-hole was not satisfactory.

378
00:40:38,271 --> 00:40:39,522
Who are you?

379
00:40:40,774 --> 00:40:42,734
How the hell did you get in here?

380
00:40:44,652 --> 00:40:47,989
What the bloody hell
do you think you're doing?

381
00:40:51,993 --> 00:40:53,787
Naughty, naughty, naughty!

382
00:40:54,037 --> 00:40:56,664
You filthy old soomaka.

383
00:40:56,915 --> 00:41:00,502
Now listen here,
you little bastard!

384
00:41:00,752 --> 00:41:04,214
Just turn round and walk out
of here the same way you came in.

385
00:41:07,425 --> 00:41:08,927
Leave that alone!
Don't touch it!

386
00:41:09,177 --> 00:41:11,596
It's a very important work of art.

387
00:41:22,399 --> 00:41:24,859
What the bloody hell do you want?

388
00:41:26,194 --> 00:41:29,072
To be perfectly honest, madam...

389
00:41:29,322 --> 00:41:32,659
...l'm taking part in an
international students' contest...

390
00:41:32,909 --> 00:41:36,663
...to see who can get the most
points for selling magazines.

391
00:41:36,913 --> 00:41:39,040
Cut the shit, sonny...

392
00:41:39,290 --> 00:41:43,837
...and get out of here before you
get yourself into serious trouble.

393
00:41:44,170 --> 00:41:47,215
I told you to leave that alone!
Now get out of here...

394
00:41:47,465 --> 00:41:49,342
...before I throw you out!

395
00:41:49,843 --> 00:41:52,679
Wretched, slummy bedbug!

396
00:41:53,221 --> 00:41:56,933
I'll teach you to break
into real people's houses.

397
00:41:58,184 --> 00:41:59,102
Fucking...

398
00:41:59,352 --> 00:42:00,353
...little...

399
00:42:00,937 --> 00:42:02,439
...bastard!

400
00:43:12,092 --> 00:43:15,053
-Let's go. The police are coming!
-One minoota, droogie.

401
00:43:21,768 --> 00:43:24,562
You bastards! I'm blind!

402
00:43:24,813 --> 00:43:28,858
I'm blind, you bastards!
I can't see!

403
00:43:42,706 --> 00:43:45,917
It's no good sitting there in hope,
my little brothers.

404
00:43:46,126 --> 00:43:50,463
I won't say a single solitary
slovo unless I have my lawyer here.

405
00:43:50,797 --> 00:43:53,341
I know the law, you bastards.

406
00:44:01,224 --> 00:44:02,892
Righty-right, Tom.

407
00:44:04,394 --> 00:44:08,273
We'll have to show our friend Alex
here that we know the law too.

408
00:44:08,565 --> 00:44:11,192
But that knowing the law
isn't everything.

409
00:44:26,041 --> 00:44:28,710
Nasty cut you've got there,
little Alex.

410
00:44:29,753 --> 00:44:31,671
Shame, isn't it?

411
00:44:32,547 --> 00:44:34,591
Spoils all your beauty.

412
00:44:36,634 --> 00:44:38,219
Who gave you that, then?

413
00:44:39,721 --> 00:44:41,389
How'd you do that, then?

414
00:44:43,933 --> 00:44:46,019
What's your point, you bastard?

415
00:44:46,269 --> 00:44:48,480
That is for your lady victim.

416
00:44:48,730 --> 00:44:49,981
You ghastly...

417
00:44:50,231 --> 00:44:51,983
...wretched scoundrel.

418
00:44:54,319 --> 00:44:55,528
Get him off me!

419
00:44:56,488 --> 00:44:58,615
You rotten little bastard!

420
00:45:06,873 --> 00:45:08,124
Good evening, Mr. Deltoid.

421
00:45:08,375 --> 00:45:10,043
Good evening, Sergeant.

422
00:45:10,293 --> 00:45:11,378
They're in room B, sir.

423
00:45:11,628 --> 00:45:13,296
Thank you very much.

424
00:45:14,297 --> 00:45:15,423
Sergeant...

425
00:45:15,674 --> 00:45:16,633
Good evening.

426
00:45:16,883 --> 00:45:18,385
Good evening, Inspector.

427
00:45:18,635 --> 00:45:21,554
-Would you like your tea now, sir?
-No, thank you, Sergeant.

428
00:45:21,805 --> 00:45:23,765
May I have some
paper towels, please?

429
00:45:24,015 --> 00:45:26,267
We're interrogating
the prisoner now.

430
00:45:26,518 --> 00:45:30,105
-Perhaps you'd care to come inside.
-Thank you very much.

431
00:45:30,730 --> 00:45:33,692
Good evening, Sergeant.
Good evening, all.

432
00:45:35,694 --> 00:45:38,780
Oh, dear! This boy
does look a mess, doesn't he?

433
00:45:39,072 --> 00:45:40,907
Just look at the state of him.

434
00:45:41,157 --> 00:45:43,118
Love's young nightmare-like.

435
00:45:43,368 --> 00:45:45,286
Violence makes violence.

436
00:45:45,537 --> 00:45:47,539
He resisted his lawful arrestors.

437
00:45:49,040 --> 00:45:52,293
This is the end of the line for me.

438
00:45:52,544 --> 00:45:55,714
The end of the line, yes.

439
00:45:56,047 --> 00:45:57,507
And what of me, brother sir?

440
00:45:57,757 --> 00:45:59,426
Speak up for me.
I'm not so bad.

441
00:45:59,718 --> 00:46:01,678
I was led on by
the treachery of others.

442
00:46:01,970 --> 00:46:04,806
Sings the roof off lovely,
he does, sir.

443
00:46:05,098 --> 00:46:08,351
Where are my treacherous droogs?
Get them before they get away!

444
00:46:08,601 --> 00:46:10,437
It was all their idea, brothers.

445
00:46:10,687 --> 00:46:13,356
They forced me to do it.
I'm innocent!

446
00:46:20,071 --> 00:46:22,824
You are now a murderer,
little Alex.

447
00:46:23,491 --> 00:46:24,826
A murderer.

448
00:46:25,618 --> 00:46:27,620
Not true, sir.

449
00:46:27,871 --> 00:46:29,664
It was only a slight tolchok.

450
00:46:29,914 --> 00:46:32,459
She were breathing, I swear it.

451
00:46:32,876 --> 00:46:35,128
I've just come from the hospital.

452
00:46:35,378 --> 00:46:37,672
Your victim has died.

453
00:46:37,922 --> 00:46:41,092
You try to frighten me.
Admit so, sir.

454
00:46:41,343 --> 00:46:43,303
This is some new form of torture.

455
00:46:43,553 --> 00:46:46,848
-Say it, brother sir.
-lt'll be your own torture.

456
00:46:47,098 --> 00:46:50,894
I hope to God
it'll torture you to madness.

457
00:46:52,729 --> 00:46:55,815
If you'd care to give him a bash
in the chops, don't mind us.

458
00:46:56,066 --> 00:46:57,859
We'll hold him down.

459
00:46:58,568 --> 00:47:01,780
He must be a great
disappointment to you, sir.

460
00:47:31,226 --> 00:47:34,896
This is the real weepy and tragic
part of the story beginning...

461
00:47:35,146 --> 00:47:37,357
...O my brothers and only friends.

462
00:47:37,607 --> 00:47:40,068
After a trial,
with judges and a jury...

463
00:47:40,318 --> 00:47:44,572
...and hard words spoken against
your friend and humble narrator...

464
00:47:44,823 --> 00:47:48,910
...he was sentenced to 14 years
in Staja Number 84-F...

465
00:47:49,160 --> 00:47:52,706
...among smelly perverts
and hardened prestoopniks.

466
00:47:52,956 --> 00:47:56,793
The shock sending my dada beating
his bruised and krovvy rookers...

467
00:47:57,043 --> 00:47:59,379
...against unfair Bog
in His Heaven.

468
00:47:59,629 --> 00:48:02,841
And my mum boo-hoo-hooing
in her mother's grief...

469
00:48:03,091 --> 00:48:05,468
...at her only child
and son of her bosom...

470
00:48:05,719 --> 00:48:08,346
...like, letting everybody down
real horrorshow.

471
00:48:08,596 --> 00:48:11,474
Morning.
One up from Thames, mister.

472
00:48:12,517 --> 00:48:14,144
Right! Open up the cell!

473
00:48:14,394 --> 00:48:15,812
Yes, sir.

474
00:48:32,120 --> 00:48:34,372
Here are the prisoner's
committal forms.

475
00:48:34,622 --> 00:48:36,124
Thank you, mister.

476
00:48:37,751 --> 00:48:40,462
-Name?
-Alexander DeLarge.

477
00:48:40,712 --> 00:48:42,630
You are now in
H.M. Prison Parkmoor.

478
00:48:42,881 --> 00:48:46,426
From this moment, you will address
all prison officers as "sir."

479
00:48:46,676 --> 00:48:47,510
Name?

480
00:48:47,719 --> 00:48:50,096
Alexander DeLarge, sir.

481
00:48:50,347 --> 00:48:51,389
Sentence?

482
00:48:51,639 --> 00:48:52,849
14 years, sir.

483
00:48:53,099 --> 00:48:53,975
Crime?

484
00:48:54,225 --> 00:48:55,352
Murder, sir.

485
00:48:55,602 --> 00:48:58,563
Right.
Take the cuffs off him, mister.

486
00:49:09,866 --> 00:49:12,243
You are now 655321 .

487
00:49:12,494 --> 00:49:15,789
It is your duty
to memorize that number.

488
00:49:16,039 --> 00:49:18,083
Thank you, mister. Well done.

489
00:49:18,333 --> 00:49:20,043
-Thank you.
-Let the officer out.

490
00:49:24,339 --> 00:49:26,841
All right, empty your pockets.

491
00:49:30,553 --> 00:49:33,682
Are you able to see the white line
painted on the floor...

492
00:49:33,932 --> 00:49:35,266
...directly behind you...

493
00:49:35,517 --> 00:49:36,851
...655321?

494
00:49:39,354 --> 00:49:40,772
Then your toes belong...

495
00:49:41,022 --> 00:49:42,982
...on the other side of it!

496
00:49:49,989 --> 00:49:51,700
-Yes, sir.
-Right.

497
00:49:52,117 --> 00:49:53,451
Carry on.

498
00:49:58,289 --> 00:49:59,207
Pick that up...

499
00:49:59,457 --> 00:50:02,252
...and put it down properly.

500
00:50:13,054 --> 00:50:15,056
One half-bar of chocolate.

501
00:50:17,058 --> 00:50:20,020
One bunch of keys
on white metal ring.

502
00:50:23,064 --> 00:50:25,025
One packet of cigarettes.

503
00:50:28,236 --> 00:50:30,321
Two plastic ball pens.

504
00:50:30,572 --> 00:50:32,657
One black, one red.

505
00:50:35,869 --> 00:50:39,080
One pocket comb, black plastic.

506
00:50:39,664 --> 00:50:44,210
One address book,
imitation red leather.

507
00:50:52,969 --> 00:50:54,929
One ten-penny piece.

508
00:50:56,348 --> 00:50:59,017
One white metal wristlet watch...

509
00:50:59,267 --> 00:51:03,229
...Timawrist, on a white metal
expanding bracelet.

510
00:51:04,397 --> 00:51:06,316
Anything else in your pockets?

511
00:51:07,359 --> 00:51:08,860
-No, sir.
-Right.

512
00:51:09,110 --> 00:51:12,238
Sign here for your
valuable property.

513
00:51:21,081 --> 00:51:23,166
The tobacco and chocolate
you brought in...

514
00:51:23,416 --> 00:51:24,709
...you lose that...

515
00:51:24,959 --> 00:51:27,045
...as you are now convicted.

516
00:51:27,921 --> 00:51:31,132
Now over to the table
and get undressed.

517
00:51:38,181 --> 00:51:40,183
Were you in police custody
this morning?

518
00:51:40,433 --> 00:51:41,935
One jacket, blue pinstriped.

519
00:51:42,185 --> 00:51:43,269
Prison custody?

520
00:51:43,520 --> 00:51:44,562
Yes, sir, on remand.

521
00:51:44,813 --> 00:51:46,648
-One necktie, blue.
-Religion?

522
00:51:46,940 --> 00:51:48,024
C. of E., sir.

523
00:51:48,274 --> 00:51:49,943
Do you mean the Church of England?

524
00:51:50,193 --> 00:51:51,945
Yes, sir.
The Church of England.

525
00:51:52,195 --> 00:51:53,196
Brown hair, isn't it?

526
00:51:53,446 --> 00:51:54,614
Fair hair, sir.

527
00:51:54,864 --> 00:51:55,865
Blue eyes?

528
00:51:56,116 --> 00:51:57,534
Blue, sir.

529
00:51:57,784 --> 00:52:00,370
Do you wear eyeglasses
or contact lenses?

530
00:52:00,620 --> 00:52:01,454
No, sir.

531
00:52:01,705 --> 00:52:03,665
One shirt, blue.
Collar attached.

532
00:52:03,915 --> 00:52:07,669
Have you been receiving medical
treatment for any serious illness?

533
00:52:07,919 --> 00:52:10,422
One pair of boots, black leather.
Zippered. Worn.

534
00:52:10,672 --> 00:52:13,216
Have you ever had
any mental illness?

535
00:52:13,633 --> 00:52:17,345
Do you wear any false teeth
or any false limbs?

536
00:52:17,762 --> 00:52:19,806
One pair of trousers,
blue pinstriped.

537
00:52:20,056 --> 00:52:23,435
Have you ever had any attacks
of fainting or dizziness?

538
00:52:23,685 --> 00:52:25,228
One pair of socks, black.

539
00:52:25,478 --> 00:52:27,230
Are you an epileptic?

540
00:52:27,480 --> 00:52:30,025
One pair of underpants,
white with blue waistband.

541
00:52:30,233 --> 00:52:33,945
Are you now, or have you ever been,
a homosexual?

542
00:52:34,404 --> 00:52:35,280
Right.

543
00:52:35,530 --> 00:52:38,074
-The mothballs, mister.
-Mothballs, sir.

544
00:52:39,034 --> 00:52:40,410
Now then, face the wall...

545
00:52:40,827 --> 00:52:43,496
...bend over and touch your toes.

546
00:52:50,086 --> 00:52:51,629
Any venereal disease?

547
00:52:51,880 --> 00:52:53,381
Crabs? Lice?

548
00:52:53,631 --> 00:52:56,634
-Through there for the bath.
-One for a bath.

549
00:52:58,678 --> 00:52:59,971
What's it going to be, eh?

550
00:53:00,847 --> 00:53:04,351
Is it going to be in and out
of institutions like this...

551
00:53:04,601 --> 00:53:06,603
...though more in than out
for most of you?

552
00:53:06,853 --> 00:53:10,940
Or are you going to attend
to the divine word...

553
00:53:11,191 --> 00:53:14,903
...and realize the punishments
that await unrepentant sinners...

554
00:53:15,153 --> 00:53:17,238
...in the next world
as well as this?

555
00:53:17,489 --> 00:53:19,532
A lot of idiots you are...

556
00:53:19,783 --> 00:53:24,454
...selling your birthright
for a saucer of cold porridge.

557
00:53:24,704 --> 00:53:26,414
The thrill of theft.

558
00:53:26,664 --> 00:53:27,499
Of violence.

559
00:53:27,749 --> 00:53:30,418
The urge to live easy.

560
00:53:30,669 --> 00:53:33,338
Well, I ask you what is it worth...

561
00:53:33,588 --> 00:53:35,924
...when we have undeniable proof...

562
00:53:36,174 --> 00:53:39,302
...yes, incontrovertible
evidence...

563
00:53:39,552 --> 00:53:40,887
...that hell exists?

564
00:53:41,137 --> 00:53:42,347
I know!

565
00:53:42,597 --> 00:53:45,141
I know, my friends.

566
00:53:45,392 --> 00:53:47,477
I have been informed...

567
00:53:47,727 --> 00:53:49,229
...in visions...

568
00:53:49,479 --> 00:53:50,939
...that there is a place...

569
00:53:51,189 --> 00:53:53,608
...darker than any prison...

570
00:53:53,858 --> 00:53:57,904
...hotter than any flame
of human fire...

571
00:53:58,154 --> 00:53:59,489
...where souls...

572
00:53:59,739 --> 00:54:03,952
...of unrepentant criminal sinners
like yourselves...

573
00:54:05,829 --> 00:54:09,499
Don't you laugh, damn you!
Don't you laugh.

574
00:54:09,749 --> 00:54:12,752
I say, like yourselves...

575
00:54:13,294 --> 00:54:14,587
...scream...

576
00:54:15,005 --> 00:54:18,675
...in endless and
unendurable agony.

577
00:54:19,426 --> 00:54:20,802
Their skin...

578
00:54:21,052 --> 00:54:23,555
...rotting and peeling.

579
00:54:23,805 --> 00:54:25,557
A fireball...

580
00:54:25,807 --> 00:54:28,143
...spinning in their
screaming guts!

581
00:54:28,393 --> 00:54:31,813
I know. Yes, I know!

582
00:54:38,111 --> 00:54:41,114
All right, you lot!
We'll end by singing hymn 258...

583
00:54:41,364 --> 00:54:42,657
...in the prisoner's hymnal.

584
00:54:42,907 --> 00:54:46,119
And let's have a little reverence,
you bastards!

585
00:54:47,787 --> 00:54:51,082
I was a wandering sheep

586
00:54:52,167 --> 00:54:54,794
-Sing up, damn you!
-I did not love the fold

587
00:54:55,045 --> 00:54:56,463
Louder!

588
00:54:58,798 --> 00:55:03,803
I did not love my shepherd's voice

589
00:55:04,429 --> 00:55:08,808
I would not be controlled

590
00:55:09,934 --> 00:55:11,061
Louder!

591
00:55:11,519 --> 00:55:14,564
It had not been edifying.
Indeed not.

592
00:55:14,814 --> 00:55:18,735
Being in this hellhole
and human zoo for two years now.

593
00:55:18,985 --> 00:55:22,113
Being kicked and tolchoked
by brutal warders...

594
00:55:22,364 --> 00:55:25,325
...and meeting leering criminals
and perverts...

595
00:55:25,575 --> 00:55:27,118
...ready to dribble all over...

596
00:55:27,369 --> 00:55:30,288
...a luscious young malchick
like your storyteller.

597
00:55:36,294 --> 00:55:37,796
It was my rabbit...

598
00:55:38,046 --> 00:55:40,799
...to help the prison charlie
with the Sunday service.

599
00:55:41,049 --> 00:55:44,094
He was a bolshy,
great burly bastard.

600
00:55:44,344 --> 00:55:47,389
But he was very fond of myself,
me being very young...

601
00:55:47,639 --> 00:55:51,059
...and also now very interested
in the Big Book.

602
00:56:12,163 --> 00:56:16,001
I read all about the scourging
and the crowning with thorns.

603
00:56:16,251 --> 00:56:18,128
And I could viddy myself
helping in...

604
00:56:18,378 --> 00:56:22,340
...and even taking charge of
the tolchoking and the nailing in.

605
00:56:22,590 --> 00:56:25,927
Being dressed in the height
of Roman fashion.

606
00:56:37,856 --> 00:56:40,358
I didn't so much like
the latter part of the Book...

607
00:56:40,608 --> 00:56:42,736
... which is more like
all preachy talking...

608
00:56:42,986 --> 00:56:45,155
...than fighting
and the old in-out.

609
00:56:45,405 --> 00:56:48,533
I like the parts where these old
yahoodies tolchok each other...

610
00:56:48,783 --> 00:56:51,036
...and then drink
their Hebrew vino...

611
00:56:51,411 --> 00:56:54,456
...and getting onto the bed
with their wives' handmaidens.

612
00:56:54,706 --> 00:56:56,750
That kept me going.

613
00:57:28,073 --> 00:57:30,992
"Seek not to be like evil men.

614
00:57:31,409 --> 00:57:33,536
Neither desire to be with them...

615
00:57:33,787 --> 00:57:36,873
...because their minds
studieth robberies...

616
00:57:37,123 --> 00:57:40,043
...and their lips speak deceits."

617
00:57:40,293 --> 00:57:43,797
If thou lose hope, being weary
in the days of distress...

618
00:57:44,047 --> 00:57:46,299
...thy strength
shall be diminished.

619
00:57:46,549 --> 00:57:48,218
Fine, my son. Fine.

620
00:57:48,468 --> 00:57:49,719
Father?

621
00:57:53,765 --> 00:57:55,517
I have tried, have I not?

622
00:57:55,767 --> 00:57:56,851
You have, my son.

623
00:57:57,102 --> 00:57:59,437
-I've done my best, have I not?
-lndeed.

624
00:57:59,688 --> 00:58:03,066
I've never been guilty of any
institutional infraction, have I?

625
00:58:03,316 --> 00:58:07,654
You certainly have not, 655321 .
You've been very helpful.

626
00:58:07,904 --> 00:58:10,782
And you've shown
a genuine desire to reform.

627
00:58:11,032 --> 00:58:12,325
Father...

628
00:58:13,785 --> 00:58:16,579
...can I ask you
a question in private?

629
00:58:18,206 --> 00:58:20,125
Certainly, my son. Certainly.

630
00:58:30,301 --> 00:58:32,846
Is there something
troubling you, my son?

631
00:58:35,974 --> 00:58:38,268
Don't be shy to speak up.

632
00:58:40,770 --> 00:58:42,105
Remember...

633
00:58:42,355 --> 00:58:44,315
...I know of the...

634
00:58:44,566 --> 00:58:48,403
...urges that can
trouble young men...

635
00:58:48,653 --> 00:58:50,155
...deprived...

636
00:58:50,405 --> 00:58:52,407
...of the society of women.

637
00:58:55,285 --> 00:58:57,620
It's nothing like that, Father.

638
00:59:01,374 --> 00:59:04,753
It's about this new thing
they're all talking about.

639
00:59:05,295 --> 00:59:06,963
About this new treatment.

640
00:59:07,213 --> 00:59:09,549
It gets you out of prison
in no time.

641
00:59:09,799 --> 00:59:12,385
And makes sure you
never get back in again.

642
00:59:13,178 --> 00:59:15,430
Where did you hear about this?

643
00:59:15,680 --> 00:59:18,350
Who's been talking
about these things?

644
00:59:18,641 --> 00:59:21,061
These things get around.

645
00:59:21,311 --> 00:59:23,563
Two warders talk, as it might be.

646
00:59:23,813 --> 00:59:26,858
And somebody can't help
overhearing what they say.

647
00:59:27,400 --> 00:59:30,779
Then somebody picks up a scrap
of newspaper in the workshops...

648
00:59:31,029 --> 00:59:33,615
...and the newspaper
tells all about it.

649
00:59:36,576 --> 00:59:40,288
How about putting me in
for this new treatment?

650
00:59:41,915 --> 00:59:45,585
I take it you are referring...

651
00:59:45,835 --> 00:59:48,088
...to the Ludovico technique.

652
00:59:48,838 --> 00:59:51,174
I don't know what it's called.

653
00:59:51,424 --> 00:59:53,301
I just know it
gets you out quickly...

654
00:59:53,551 --> 00:59:56,054
...and makes sure you
never get back in again.

655
00:59:56,763 --> 00:59:59,599
That is not proven, 655321 .

656
00:59:59,849 --> 01:00:04,020
In fact, it is only in the
experimental stage at this moment.

657
01:00:04,479 --> 01:00:07,232
It has been used, hasn't it?

658
01:00:07,482 --> 01:00:10,235
It has not been used
in this prison yet.

659
01:00:10,485 --> 01:00:12,946
The governor has grave
doubts about it.

660
01:00:13,196 --> 01:00:16,908
And I've heard there are
very serious dangers involved.

661
01:00:18,910 --> 01:00:21,746
I don't care about the dangers.

662
01:00:23,456 --> 01:00:25,625
I just want to be good.

663
01:00:26,876 --> 01:00:29,546
I want for the rest
of my life to be...

664
01:00:29,796 --> 01:00:31,881
...one act of goodness.

665
01:00:32,132 --> 01:00:33,591
The question is...

666
01:00:34,009 --> 01:00:38,638
...whether or not this technique
really makes a man good.

667
01:00:39,472 --> 01:00:41,766
Goodness comes from within.

668
01:00:42,017 --> 01:00:43,143
Goodness...

669
01:00:43,393 --> 01:00:44,769
...is chosen.

670
01:00:45,145 --> 01:00:47,272
When a man cannot choose...

671
01:00:47,522 --> 01:00:49,649
...he ceases to be a man.

672
01:00:51,443 --> 01:00:56,364
I don't understand about
the whys and wherefores, Father.

673
01:00:57,574 --> 01:01:00,493
I only know I want to be good.

674
01:01:02,620 --> 01:01:04,539
Be patient, my son.

675
01:01:04,789 --> 01:01:07,042
Put your trust in the Lord.

676
01:01:08,960 --> 01:01:12,547
Instruct Thy Son
and He shall refresh thee...

677
01:01:12,797 --> 01:01:15,675
...and shall give delight
to thy soul.

678
01:01:16,301 --> 01:01:17,552
Amen.

679
01:01:45,330 --> 01:01:47,290
-Mister!
-All present and correct, sir!

680
01:01:47,540 --> 01:01:48,583
Right!

681
01:01:50,168 --> 01:01:52,253
All present and correct, sir!

682
01:02:47,809 --> 01:02:49,352
Prisoners, halt!

683
01:02:49,894 --> 01:02:51,521
Now pay attention!

684
01:02:52,230 --> 01:02:53,982
I want you in two lines...

685
01:02:54,232 --> 01:02:56,901
...up against that wall,
facing this way.

686
01:02:57,152 --> 01:02:58,695
Go on, move!

687
01:02:59,195 --> 01:03:00,196
Hurry up!

688
01:03:00,447 --> 01:03:01,740
Stop talking!

689
01:03:07,579 --> 01:03:10,165
Prisoners ready
for inspection, sir!

690
01:03:26,139 --> 01:03:27,307
How many to a cell?

691
01:03:27,557 --> 01:03:29,434
Four in this block, sir.

692
01:03:30,310 --> 01:03:32,562
Cram criminals together
and what do you get?

693
01:03:32,812 --> 01:03:35,982
Concentrated criminality.
Crime in the midst of punishment.

694
01:03:36,232 --> 01:03:39,903
I agree, sir. We need
larger prisons, more money.

695
01:03:40,153 --> 01:03:41,946
Not a chance, my dear fellow.

696
01:03:42,197 --> 01:03:44,532
The government can't be
concerned any longer...

697
01:03:44,783 --> 01:03:46,493
...with outmoded
penalogical theories.

698
01:03:46,785 --> 01:03:50,413
Soon we may need all prison
space for political offenders.

699
01:03:50,663 --> 01:03:54,209
Common criminals are best dealt
with on a purely curative basis.

700
01:03:54,459 --> 01:03:57,170
Kill the criminal reflex,
that's all.

701
01:03:57,420 --> 01:03:59,631
Full implementation
in a year's time.

702
01:03:59,881 --> 01:04:02,133
Punishment means nothing to them.

703
01:04:02,384 --> 01:04:05,303
They enjoy their
so-called punishment.

704
01:04:05,595 --> 01:04:06,721
You're absolutely right, sir.

705
01:04:06,971 --> 01:04:09,557
Shut your bleeding hole!

706
01:04:10,183 --> 01:04:11,726
Who said that?

707
01:04:12,352 --> 01:04:13,770
I did, sir.

708
01:04:20,026 --> 01:04:21,736
What crime did you commit?

709
01:04:21,986 --> 01:04:24,072
The accidental killing
of a person, sir.

710
01:04:24,322 --> 01:04:27,033
He brutally murdered a woman
in furtherance of theft.

711
01:04:27,283 --> 01:04:28,910
Fourteen years, sir.

712
01:04:30,203 --> 01:04:31,371
Excellent.

713
01:04:32,914 --> 01:04:34,082
He's enterprising...

714
01:04:34,332 --> 01:04:35,417
...aggressive...

715
01:04:35,667 --> 01:04:36,835
...outgoing...

716
01:04:37,085 --> 01:04:37,919
...young...

717
01:04:38,169 --> 01:04:39,462
...bold...

718
01:04:39,713 --> 01:04:41,214
...vicious.

719
01:04:41,715 --> 01:04:42,757
He'll do.

720
01:04:43,008 --> 01:04:44,134
Fine.

721
01:04:44,384 --> 01:04:45,885
We could still look at C-block.

722
01:04:46,136 --> 01:04:48,179
No, no. That's enough.
He's perfect.

723
01:04:48,430 --> 01:04:50,140
I want his records sent to me.

724
01:04:50,390 --> 01:04:51,725
This vicious young hoodlum...

725
01:04:51,975 --> 01:04:53,893
...will be transformed
out of all recognition.

726
01:04:54,144 --> 01:04:56,104
Thank you very much
for this chance.

727
01:04:56,354 --> 01:04:59,149
Let's hope you make
the most of it, my boy.

728
01:04:59,441 --> 01:05:01,943
-Shall we go to my office?
-Thank you.

729
01:05:08,742 --> 01:05:10,035
Come in.

730
01:05:11,828 --> 01:05:12,662
Sir!

731
01:05:12,912 --> 01:05:14,789
655321 . Sir!

732
01:05:15,040 --> 01:05:16,041
Very good, Chief.

733
01:05:16,291 --> 01:05:17,834
Over to the line.
Toes behind it.

734
01:05:18,084 --> 01:05:20,587
Full name and number
to the governor.

735
01:05:21,421 --> 01:05:24,632
Alexander DeLarge, sir.
655321, sir.

736
01:05:27,302 --> 01:05:30,430
I don't suppose you know who
that was this morning.

737
01:05:30,680 --> 01:05:34,309
That was no less a personage
than the Minister of the Interior.

738
01:05:34,559 --> 01:05:36,519
The new Minister of the Interior.

739
01:05:36,770 --> 01:05:39,689
What they call a very new broom.

740
01:05:40,857 --> 01:05:44,319
These new ridiculous ideas
have come at last.

741
01:05:44,569 --> 01:05:46,863
And orders are orders...

742
01:05:47,113 --> 01:05:50,658
...though I may say to you
in confidence, I do not approve.

743
01:05:50,909 --> 01:05:53,161
An eye for an eye, I say.

744
01:05:53,411 --> 01:05:56,373
If someone hits you,
you hit back, do you not?

745
01:05:56,623 --> 01:06:00,335
Why should not the state,
severely hit by you hooligans...

746
01:06:00,585 --> 01:06:02,379
...not hit back also?

747
01:06:03,254 --> 01:06:05,215
The new view is to say "no."

748
01:06:05,465 --> 01:06:08,843
The new view is that
we turn the bad into good.

749
01:06:09,094 --> 01:06:12,055
All of which seems to me
to be grossly unjust.

750
01:06:12,472 --> 01:06:15,016
Shut your filthy hole, you scum!

751
01:06:15,475 --> 01:06:17,686
You are to be reformed.

752
01:06:18,520 --> 01:06:21,022
Tomorrow you will go
to this man, Brodsky.

753
01:06:21,272 --> 01:06:22,857
You will be leaving here.

754
01:06:23,108 --> 01:06:27,362
You will be transferred to
the Ludovico medical facility.

755
01:06:27,654 --> 01:06:31,574
It's believed you'll be able to
leave state custody in a fortnight.

756
01:06:31,825 --> 01:06:33,702
I suppose that prospect
pleases you?

757
01:06:33,952 --> 01:06:35,745
Answer the governor's question!

758
01:06:35,995 --> 01:06:37,330
Yes, sir.
Thank you very much.

759
01:06:37,580 --> 01:06:39,916
I've done my best here,
I really have, sir.

760
01:06:40,166 --> 01:06:42,419
I'm very grateful
to all concerned, sir.

761
01:06:44,629 --> 01:06:47,048
Sign this where it's marked.

762
01:06:50,218 --> 01:06:52,262
Don't read it, sign it!

763
01:06:52,554 --> 01:06:56,224
It says you're willing to have
your sentence commuted...

764
01:06:56,474 --> 01:06:59,436
...to submission to
the Ludovico treatment.

765
01:06:59,686 --> 01:07:01,021
And this.

766
01:07:08,194 --> 01:07:09,779
And another copy.

767
01:07:22,334 --> 01:07:24,169
The next morning I was taken to...

768
01:07:24,419 --> 01:07:26,087
...the Ludovico medical facility...

769
01:07:26,338 --> 01:07:28,173
...outside the town center.

770
01:07:28,423 --> 01:07:29,924
I felt a malenky bit sad...

771
01:07:30,175 --> 01:07:32,093
...having to say goodbye
to the old Staja...

772
01:07:32,344 --> 01:07:35,597
...as you will, when you leave
a place you've gotten used to.

773
01:07:35,847 --> 01:07:37,807
Right, halt the prisoner.

774
01:07:43,313 --> 01:07:45,774
Good morning, sir.
I'm Chief Officer Barnes.

775
01:07:46,024 --> 01:07:47,817
I've got 655321 ...

776
01:07:48,068 --> 01:07:51,738
...on a transfer from Parkmoor
to the Ludovico Centre, sir.

777
01:07:52,072 --> 01:07:54,657
Good morning.
Yes, we've been expecting you.

778
01:07:54,908 --> 01:07:56,201
I'm Dr. Alcot.

779
01:07:58,495 --> 01:07:59,454
Dr. Alcot.

780
01:07:59,704 --> 01:08:01,081
Very good, sir.

781
01:08:04,834 --> 01:08:07,962
-Are you prepared for the prisoner?
-Yes, of course.

782
01:08:08,213 --> 01:08:12,217
I wonder if you'd mind signing
these documents, sir.

783
01:08:13,093 --> 01:08:14,511
There, sir.

784
01:08:25,980 --> 01:08:27,399
And there, sir.

785
01:08:32,862 --> 01:08:34,447
And there.

786
01:08:53,383 --> 01:08:54,926
There you are.

787
01:08:57,053 --> 01:08:58,972
Prison escort, move forward!

788
01:09:02,142 --> 01:09:03,309
Halt!

789
01:09:05,395 --> 01:09:07,105
Excuse me, sir.

790
01:09:13,653 --> 01:09:16,906
Is that the officer who will
take charge of the prisoner?

791
01:09:26,458 --> 01:09:29,961
A word of advice, doc.
You'll have to watch this one.

792
01:09:30,211 --> 01:09:33,757
A right brutal bastard he has been,
and will be again...

793
01:09:34,007 --> 01:09:37,177
...in spite of all his sucking up
and reading the Bible.

794
01:09:37,427 --> 01:09:41,097
We can manage things.
Show the young man to his room.

795
01:09:41,348 --> 01:09:44,100
Right, sir. Come this way, please.

796
01:09:52,859 --> 01:09:55,445
-Morning, Charlie.
-Good morning, Doctor.

797
01:09:56,696 --> 01:09:57,739
Good morning, Alex.

798
01:09:57,989 --> 01:10:00,575
My name is Dr. Branom.
I'm Dr. Brodsky's assistant.

799
01:10:00,825 --> 01:10:02,452
Good morning, missus.
Lovely day.

800
01:10:02,702 --> 01:10:03,953
Indeed, it is.

801
01:10:04,204 --> 01:10:05,789
May I take that?

802
01:10:09,459 --> 01:10:11,961
-How are you feeling?
-Fine, fine.

803
01:10:12,212 --> 01:10:15,173
Good. In a few minutes
you'll meet Dr. Brodsky...

804
01:10:15,423 --> 01:10:16,716
...and begin your treatment.

805
01:10:17,258 --> 01:10:19,844
You're a very lucky boy
to have been chosen.

806
01:10:21,763 --> 01:10:24,307
I realize that,
and I'm very grateful.

807
01:10:24,641 --> 01:10:26,768
We're going to be friends,
aren't we?

808
01:10:27,018 --> 01:10:28,353
I hope so, missus.

809
01:10:31,481 --> 01:10:33,900
What's the hypo for?
Sending me to sleep?

810
01:10:34,150 --> 01:10:35,443
Nothing of the sort.

811
01:10:35,902 --> 01:10:38,613
-Vitamins will it be, then?
-Something like that.

812
01:10:39,114 --> 01:10:43,076
You're undernourished, so after
each meal we'll give you a shot.

813
01:10:43,326 --> 01:10:44,786
Roll over on your right side.

814
01:10:45,036 --> 01:10:47,872
Loosen your pajama pants
and pull them halfway down.

815
01:10:57,799 --> 01:11:00,844
What exactly is the treatment here
going to be, then?

816
01:11:01,928 --> 01:11:03,763
It's quite simple, really.

817
01:11:04,347 --> 01:11:06,141
We're going to show you some films.

818
01:11:06,391 --> 01:11:08,727
You mean like
going to the pictures?

819
01:11:09,185 --> 01:11:10,812
Something like that.

820
01:11:11,062 --> 01:11:11,896
That's good.

821
01:11:12,147 --> 01:11:14,941
I like to viddy
the old films now and again.

822
01:11:16,985 --> 01:11:19,446
And viddy films I would.

823
01:11:19,946 --> 01:11:21,906
Where I was taken to, brothers...

824
01:11:22,157 --> 01:11:24,325
... was like no cine
I ever viddied before.

825
01:11:24,743 --> 01:11:26,870
I was bound up
in a straitjacket...

826
01:11:27,120 --> 01:11:29,330
...and my gulliver was strapped
to a headrest...

827
01:11:29,581 --> 01:11:31,875
... with wires running away from it.

828
01:11:32,125 --> 01:11:34,419
Then they clamped, like,
lid-locks on me eyes...

829
01:11:34,669 --> 01:11:38,131
...so that I could not shut them,
no matter how hard I tried.

830
01:11:38,381 --> 01:11:40,133
It seemed a bit crazy to me...

831
01:11:40,383 --> 01:11:43,261
...but I let them get on with
what they wanted to get on with.

832
01:11:43,511 --> 01:11:46,890
If I was to be a free malchick
again in a fortnight...

833
01:11:47,140 --> 01:11:50,560
...I would put up with much
in the meantime, O my brothers.

834
01:12:16,044 --> 01:12:19,381
The first film was a very good,
professional piece of cine...

835
01:12:19,631 --> 01:12:21,549
...like it was done in Hollywood.

836
01:12:21,800 --> 01:12:23,927
The sounds were real horrorshow.

837
01:12:24,177 --> 01:12:27,347
You could slooshy the screams
and moans very realistic.

838
01:12:27,597 --> 01:12:29,891
You could even get
the breathing and panting...

839
01:12:30,141 --> 01:12:33,103
...of the tolchocking malchicks
at the same time.

840
01:12:33,353 --> 01:12:35,230
And then what do you know?

841
01:12:35,480 --> 01:12:37,607
Soon our dear old friend...

842
01:12:37,857 --> 01:12:39,859
...the red, red vino on tap...

843
01:12:40,110 --> 01:12:41,236
...the same in all places...

844
01:12:41,486 --> 01:12:42,946
...like it's put out
by the same firm...

845
01:12:43,530 --> 01:12:45,115
...began to flow.

846
01:12:45,365 --> 01:12:47,534
It was beautiful.

847
01:12:47,909 --> 01:12:50,203
It's funny how the colors
of the real world...

848
01:12:50,620 --> 01:12:52,455
...only seem really real...

849
01:12:52,706 --> 01:12:54,916
... when you viddy them
on a screen.

850
01:12:57,836 --> 01:13:00,296
Now, all the time
I was watching this...

851
01:13:00,547 --> 01:13:02,799
...I was beginning
to get very aware...

852
01:13:03,049 --> 01:13:05,218
...of, like, not feeling
all that well.

853
01:13:05,468 --> 01:13:09,347
And this I put down
to all the rich food and vitamins.

854
01:13:09,597 --> 01:13:13,935
But I tried to forget this,
concentrating on the next film...

855
01:13:14,185 --> 01:13:16,855
... which jumped right away
on a young devotchka...

856
01:13:17,105 --> 01:13:19,941
... who was being given
the old in-out, in-out...

857
01:13:20,817 --> 01:13:22,944
...first by one malchick...

858
01:13:23,737 --> 01:13:24,946
...then another.

859
01:13:25,947 --> 01:13:27,532
Then another.

860
01:13:30,493 --> 01:13:32,912
When it came to
the 6th or 7th malchick...

861
01:13:33,163 --> 01:13:36,666
...leering and smecking
and then going into it...

862
01:13:36,916 --> 01:13:40,128
...I began to feel really sick.

863
01:13:40,670 --> 01:13:43,256
But I could not shut me glazzies.

864
01:13:43,506 --> 01:13:46,926
And even if I tried to move
my glazzballs about...

865
01:13:47,177 --> 01:13:49,179
...I still could not get out of...

866
01:13:49,429 --> 01:13:52,098
...the line of fire
of this picture.

867
01:13:54,851 --> 01:13:56,436
Get me up.

868
01:13:56,811 --> 01:13:58,605
I'm going to be sick.

869
01:13:59,606 --> 01:14:01,649
Get something for me to be sick in!

870
01:14:05,945 --> 01:14:08,782
Very soon now,
the drug will cause the subject...

871
01:14:09,032 --> 01:14:11,284
...to experience
a deathlike paralysis...

872
01:14:11,534 --> 01:14:15,372
...together with deep feelings
of terror and helplessness.

873
01:14:16,247 --> 01:14:20,085
One of our early test subjects
described it as being like death.

874
01:14:20,335 --> 01:14:23,254
A sense of stifling or drowning.

875
01:14:24,005 --> 01:14:26,675
And it is during this period,
we have found...

876
01:14:26,925 --> 01:14:30,553
...the subject will make
his most rewarding associations...

877
01:14:30,804 --> 01:14:34,557
...between his catastrophic
experience, environment...

878
01:14:34,808 --> 01:14:37,519
...and the violence he sees.

879
01:14:39,604 --> 01:14:41,564
Dr. Brodsky is pleased with you.

880
01:14:41,815 --> 01:14:44,192
You've made
a very positive response.

881
01:14:45,318 --> 01:14:49,197
Tomorrow there will be two
sessions, morning and afternoon.

882
01:14:49,447 --> 01:14:52,450
You mean I have to viddy
two sessions in one day?

883
01:14:52,701 --> 01:14:55,870
I imagine you'll feel a bit
limp by the end of the day.

884
01:14:56,121 --> 01:14:59,457
But we have to be hard on you.
You have to be cured.

885
01:14:59,708 --> 01:15:00,750
It was horrible.

886
01:15:01,001 --> 01:15:02,585
Of course it was horrible.

887
01:15:02,836 --> 01:15:05,255
Violence is a very horrible thing.

888
01:15:05,505 --> 01:15:07,215
That's what you're learning now.

889
01:15:07,465 --> 01:15:08,717
Your body's learning it.

890
01:15:09,342 --> 01:15:12,095
I just don't understand about
feeling sick the way I did.

891
01:15:12,345 --> 01:15:15,598
I never used to feel sick.
I used to feel the very opposite.

892
01:15:15,849 --> 01:15:18,768
Doing it or watching it,
I used to feel real horrorshow.

893
01:15:19,686 --> 01:15:23,148
You felt ill this afternoon
because you're getting better.

894
01:15:23,398 --> 01:15:26,568
When we're healthy,
we respond to the hateful...

895
01:15:26,818 --> 01:15:28,820
...with fear and nausea.

896
01:15:29,070 --> 01:15:31,239
You're becoming healthy,
that's all.

897
01:15:31,489 --> 01:15:34,576
By this time tomorrow,
you'll be healthier still.

898
01:16:27,253 --> 01:16:29,297
It was the next day, brothers...

899
01:16:29,547 --> 01:16:31,091
...and I had truly done my best...

900
01:16:31,341 --> 01:16:33,802
...morning and afternoon
to play it their way...

901
01:16:34,052 --> 01:16:36,805
...and sit like a horrorshow
cooperative malchick...

902
01:16:37,055 --> 01:16:38,556
...in the chair of torture...

903
01:16:38,807 --> 01:16:43,061
... while they flashed nasty bits
of ultra-violence on the screen...

904
01:16:43,520 --> 01:16:47,982
...though not on the soundtrack,
the only sound being music.

905
01:16:48,983 --> 01:16:51,569
Then I noticed,
in all my pain and sickness...

906
01:16:51,820 --> 01:16:55,740
... what music it was
that, like, cracked and boomed.

907
01:16:56,658 --> 01:16:59,160
It was Ludwig van.

908
01:16:59,703 --> 01:17:02,247
Ninth Symphony, fourth movement.

909
01:17:17,929 --> 01:17:20,974
Stop it! Stop it!
Please, I beg you!

910
01:17:21,474 --> 01:17:22,726
It's a sin!

911
01:17:23,101 --> 01:17:24,686
It's a sin!

912
01:17:30,191 --> 01:17:31,276
Sin?

913
01:17:31,526 --> 01:17:33,111
What's all this about sin?

914
01:17:33,611 --> 01:17:34,487
That!

915
01:17:34,738 --> 01:17:38,742
Using Ludwig van like that.
He did no harm to anyone.

916
01:17:38,992 --> 01:17:41,411
Beethoven just wrote music.

917
01:17:42,078 --> 01:17:45,248
Are you referring
to the background score?

918
01:17:46,833 --> 01:17:48,752
You've heard Beethoven before?

919
01:17:50,962 --> 01:17:52,839
So you're keen on music?

920
01:17:58,219 --> 01:17:59,971
Can't be helped.

921
01:18:00,764 --> 01:18:03,558
Here's the punishment
element perhaps.

922
01:18:04,559 --> 01:18:06,686
The governor ought to be pleased.

923
01:18:09,439 --> 01:18:11,358
I'm sorry, Alex.

924
01:18:11,649 --> 01:18:13,401
This is for your own good.

925
01:18:13,651 --> 01:18:16,029
You'll have to bear with us
for a while.

926
01:18:16,821 --> 01:18:20,533
But it's not fair.
It's not fair I should feel ill...

927
01:18:20,742 --> 01:18:23,703
...when I hear lovely,
lovely Ludwig van.

928
01:18:24,245 --> 01:18:26,581
You must take your chance, boy.

929
01:18:27,040 --> 01:18:29,542
The choice has been all yours.

930
01:18:31,044 --> 01:18:33,797
You needn't take it
any further, sir.

931
01:18:34,130 --> 01:18:37,050
You've proved to me all this
ultra-violence and killing...

932
01:18:37,300 --> 01:18:40,553
...is wrong, wrong
and terribly wrong!

933
01:18:40,970 --> 01:18:42,722
I've learned me lesson, sir.

934
01:18:42,972 --> 01:18:45,892
I see now what I've
never seen before.

935
01:18:46,142 --> 01:18:49,104
I'm cured. Praise God!

936
01:18:49,396 --> 01:18:51,815
You're not cured yet, boy.

937
01:18:52,691 --> 01:18:54,109
But, sirs.

938
01:18:54,359 --> 01:18:55,735
Missus!

939
01:18:56,069 --> 01:18:58,196
I see that it's wrong!

940
01:18:58,446 --> 01:19:02,492
It's wrong because
it's, like, against society.

941
01:19:02,742 --> 01:19:05,412
Because everybody has the
right to live and be happy...

942
01:19:05,662 --> 01:19:08,456
...without being
tolchocked and knifed!

943
01:19:08,707 --> 01:19:11,793
No, no, boy.
You really must leave it to us.

944
01:19:12,043 --> 01:19:13,712
But be cheerful about it.

945
01:19:13,962 --> 01:19:17,257
In less than a fortnight now,
you'll be a free man.

946
01:19:55,670 --> 01:19:56,880
Ladies and gentlemen...

947
01:19:57,130 --> 01:20:00,008
...at this stage, we introduce
the subject himself.

948
01:20:00,258 --> 01:20:03,219
He is, as you will perceive,
fit and well-nourished.

949
01:20:03,470 --> 01:20:06,306
He comes straight from a night's
sleep and a good breakfast...

950
01:20:06,556 --> 01:20:07,557
...undrugged...

951
01:20:07,807 --> 01:20:09,642
...unhypnotized.

952
01:20:09,893 --> 01:20:13,563
Tomorrow we send him out with
confidence into the world again...

953
01:20:13,813 --> 01:20:17,442
...as decent a lad as you
would meet on a May morning.

954
01:20:18,276 --> 01:20:21,029
What a change is here,
ladies and gentlemen.

955
01:20:21,279 --> 01:20:23,656
From the hoodlum
the state committed...

956
01:20:23,865 --> 01:20:26,659
...to unprofitable punishment
two years ago.

957
01:20:26,868 --> 01:20:29,662
Unchanged after two years.

958
01:20:30,413 --> 01:20:32,624
Unchanged, do I say?

959
01:20:32,874 --> 01:20:34,292
Not quite.

960
01:20:34,542 --> 01:20:39,297
Prison taught him the false smile,
the rubbed hands of hypocrisy.

961
01:20:39,547 --> 01:20:42,842
The fawning, greased,
obsequious leer.

962
01:20:43,343 --> 01:20:45,220
Other vices it taught him...

963
01:20:45,470 --> 01:20:49,349
...as well as confirming him in
those he had long practiced before.

964
01:20:50,558 --> 01:20:53,603
Our party promised
to restore law and order...

965
01:20:53,853 --> 01:20:57,899
...and to make the streets safe for
the ordinary peace-loving citizen.

966
01:20:58,149 --> 01:21:02,195
This pledge is now
about to become a reality.

967
01:21:02,445 --> 01:21:06,157
Ladies and gentlemen,
today is an historic moment.

968
01:21:06,408 --> 01:21:10,912
The problem of criminal violence
is soon to be a thing of the past.

969
01:21:11,913 --> 01:21:13,832
But enough of words.

970
01:21:14,082 --> 01:21:16,334
Actions speak louder than.

971
01:21:16,584 --> 01:21:18,253
Action now.

972
01:21:18,753 --> 01:21:20,714
Observe all.

973
01:21:30,348 --> 01:21:32,892
Our necks are out
a long way on this, Minister.

974
01:21:33,143 --> 01:21:35,270
I have complete faith in Brodsky.

975
01:21:35,520 --> 01:21:38,690
If the polls are right,
we have nothing to lose.

976
01:21:47,824 --> 01:21:50,160
Hello, heap of dirt.

977
01:21:52,954 --> 01:21:57,250
You don't wash much, do you,
judging by the horrible smell.

978
01:21:57,792 --> 01:22:00,253
Why do you say that?
I had a shower this morning.

979
01:22:00,503 --> 01:22:03,131
He had a shower this morning.

980
01:22:03,631 --> 01:22:05,717
You trying to call me a liar?

981
01:22:05,967 --> 01:22:06,801
No, brother.

982
01:22:07,177 --> 01:22:10,263
You must think I'm awfully stupid.

983
01:22:15,935 --> 01:22:17,729
Why did you do that, brother?

984
01:22:17,979 --> 01:22:19,939
I've never done wrong to you.

985
01:22:20,190 --> 01:22:22,275
You want to know why I did that?

986
01:22:22,692 --> 01:22:23,735
Well, you see...

987
01:22:23,985 --> 01:22:25,236
...I do this...

988
01:22:25,487 --> 01:22:26,696
...and that...

989
01:22:26,946 --> 01:22:30,158
...and this because I don't like
your horrible type, do I?

990
01:22:30,408 --> 01:22:32,744
And if you want
to start something...

991
01:22:32,994 --> 01:22:35,497
...you just go ahead.
Go on!

992
01:22:35,747 --> 01:22:36,956
Please do!

993
01:22:38,583 --> 01:22:40,418
I'm going to be sick.

994
01:22:41,252 --> 01:22:42,921
You're going to be sick, are you?

995
01:22:43,171 --> 01:22:45,548
I'm going to be sick.
Please let me get up.

996
01:22:46,299 --> 01:22:47,884
You want to get up?

997
01:22:48,301 --> 01:22:50,011
Well, now you listen to me.

998
01:22:50,720 --> 01:22:52,305
If you want to get up...

999
01:22:52,806 --> 01:22:54,766
...you've got to
do something for me.

1000
01:22:55,475 --> 01:22:56,643
Here.

1001
01:22:57,143 --> 01:22:58,269
Here.

1002
01:22:58,978 --> 01:23:00,647
You see that?

1003
01:23:01,648 --> 01:23:03,108
You see that shoe?

1004
01:23:04,442 --> 01:23:05,902
I want you to lick it.

1005
01:23:06,152 --> 01:23:07,445
Go on!

1006
01:23:08,488 --> 01:23:09,989
Lick it!

1007
01:23:13,076 --> 01:23:15,412
And, O my brothers,
would you believe...

1008
01:23:15,662 --> 01:23:18,957
...your faithful friend
and long-suffering narrator...

1009
01:23:19,207 --> 01:23:21,626
...pushed out his red yabzick
a mile and a half...

1010
01:23:21,876 --> 01:23:24,713
...to lick the grahzny,
vonny boots.

1011
01:23:25,505 --> 01:23:26,506
And again!

1012
01:23:26,756 --> 01:23:29,217
The horrible killing sickness
had whooshed up...

1013
01:23:29,467 --> 01:23:31,094
...and turned the joy of battle...

1014
01:23:31,886 --> 01:23:34,514
...into a feeling
I was going to snuff it.

1015
01:23:34,764 --> 01:23:36,057
And again.

1016
01:23:36,558 --> 01:23:38,560
Nice and clean.

1017
01:23:41,187 --> 01:23:42,355
Thank you very much.

1018
01:23:42,605 --> 01:23:44,441
That will do very well.

1019
01:23:48,653 --> 01:23:50,947
Thank you very much,
ladies and gentlemen.

1020
01:25:01,393 --> 01:25:03,103
She came towards me...

1021
01:25:03,353 --> 01:25:07,107
... with the light, like it was the
light light of heavenly grace.

1022
01:25:07,357 --> 01:25:09,567
And the thing that flashed
in me gulliver...

1023
01:25:09,818 --> 01:25:12,445
... was that I'd like to have her
there on the floor...

1024
01:25:12,696 --> 01:25:15,907
... with the old in-out,
real savage.

1025
01:25:32,007 --> 01:25:34,384
But quick as a shot
came the sickness.

1026
01:25:34,634 --> 01:25:37,178
Like a detective who'd been
watching around the corner...

1027
01:25:37,971 --> 01:25:40,724
...and now followed
to make his arrest.

1028
01:25:53,820 --> 01:25:54,696
Enough!

1029
01:25:55,030 --> 01:25:56,656
Thank you very much.

1030
01:25:56,906 --> 01:25:58,658
Thank you, my dear.

1031
01:26:20,513 --> 01:26:23,183
Not feeling too bad now, are you?

1032
01:26:23,600 --> 01:26:25,852
No, sir.
I feel really great, sir.

1033
01:26:26,102 --> 01:26:28,021
-Good.
-Was it all right, sir?

1034
01:26:28,271 --> 01:26:29,105
Did I do well?

1035
01:26:29,356 --> 01:26:32,692
Fine, my boy.
Absolutely fine.

1036
01:26:32,942 --> 01:26:34,194
You see, ladies and gentlemen...

1037
01:26:34,444 --> 01:26:36,905
...our subject is impelled
towards the good...

1038
01:26:37,155 --> 01:26:40,825
...by paradoxically
being impelled towards evil.

1039
01:26:41,076 --> 01:26:42,786
The intention to act violently...

1040
01:26:43,036 --> 01:26:46,414
...is accompanied by strong
feelings of physical distress.

1041
01:26:46,664 --> 01:26:49,376
To counter these,
the subject has to switch...

1042
01:26:49,626 --> 01:26:52,587
...to a diametrically
opposed attitude.

1043
01:26:53,254 --> 01:26:54,631
Any questions?

1044
01:26:54,881 --> 01:26:56,299
Choice!

1045
01:26:59,761 --> 01:27:03,264
The boy has no real choice, has he?

1046
01:27:03,515 --> 01:27:05,058
Self-interest.

1047
01:27:05,308 --> 01:27:07,185
The fear of physical pain...

1048
01:27:07,435 --> 01:27:11,981
...drove him to that
grotesque act of self-abasement.

1049
01:27:12,691 --> 01:27:14,776
Its insincerity
was clearly to be seen.

1050
01:27:15,026 --> 01:27:16,903
He ceases to be a wrongdoer.

1051
01:27:17,153 --> 01:27:21,741
He ceases also to be
a creature capable of moral choice.

1052
01:27:21,991 --> 01:27:24,327
Padre, these are subtleties.

1053
01:27:24,577 --> 01:27:27,706
We're not concerned with motives,
with the higher ethics.

1054
01:27:27,956 --> 01:27:31,626
We are concerned only
with cutting down crime.

1055
01:27:33,962 --> 01:27:38,550
And with relieving the ghastly
congestion in our prisons.

1056
01:27:39,134 --> 01:27:41,594
He will be your true Christian...

1057
01:27:41,845 --> 01:27:43,930
...ready to turn the other cheek.

1058
01:27:44,180 --> 01:27:47,183
Ready to be crucified,
rather than crucify.

1059
01:27:47,434 --> 01:27:51,563
Sick to the very heart at the
thought even of killing a fly.

1060
01:27:51,813 --> 01:27:53,148
Reclamation.

1061
01:27:53,398 --> 01:27:55,650
Joy before the angels of God.

1062
01:27:55,900 --> 01:27:59,029
The point is that it works!

1063
01:28:03,408 --> 01:28:06,745
And the very next day,
your friend and humble narrator...

1064
01:28:06,995 --> 01:28:09,039
... was a free man.

1065
01:28:47,452 --> 01:28:48,870
Son!

1066
01:28:50,455 --> 01:28:52,749
Hi, hi, hi there, my Pee and Em.

1067
01:28:54,084 --> 01:28:55,335
Mum.

1068
01:28:57,170 --> 01:28:59,506
How are you, love?
Nice to see you.

1069
01:29:01,174 --> 01:29:03,510
-Dad.
-Lad. What a surprise.

1070
01:29:03,760 --> 01:29:05,845
-Good to see you.
-Keeping fit?

1071
01:29:06,596 --> 01:29:07,847
How are you, then?

1072
01:29:08,098 --> 01:29:10,225
I'm fine, fine.

1073
01:29:10,475 --> 01:29:12,435
Keeping out of trouble, you know.

1074
01:29:15,188 --> 01:29:16,898
I'm back!

1075
01:29:19,651 --> 01:29:20,652
Good to see you.

1076
01:29:20,902 --> 01:29:24,030
Why didn't you let us know
what was happening?

1077
01:29:24,406 --> 01:29:27,534
I wanted it to be, like,
a big surprise for you and Pee.

1078
01:29:27,826 --> 01:29:30,704
It's a surprise, all right.
A bit bewildering too.

1079
01:29:30,954 --> 01:29:33,790
We've only just read about it
in morning papers.

1080
01:29:34,040 --> 01:29:35,834
You should have let us know, lad.

1081
01:29:36,501 --> 01:29:40,422
Not that we're not very pleased
to see you again, and all...

1082
01:29:40,672 --> 01:29:42,173
...cured too, eh?

1083
01:29:42,424 --> 01:29:44,509
That's right.
They did a great job on me.

1084
01:29:44,759 --> 01:29:47,387
I'm completely reformed.

1085
01:29:51,099 --> 01:29:52,809
Still the same old place, then?

1086
01:30:05,321 --> 01:30:08,158
There's a strange fellow
sitting on the sofa...

1087
01:30:08,408 --> 01:30:11,536
...munchy-wunching
lomticks of toast.

1088
01:30:14,539 --> 01:30:16,291
That's Joe.

1089
01:30:18,209 --> 01:30:20,170
He lives here now.

1090
01:30:20,462 --> 01:30:21,796
The lodger.

1091
01:30:22,047 --> 01:30:23,631
That's what he is.

1092
01:30:24,049 --> 01:30:26,051
He rents your room.

1093
01:30:36,728 --> 01:30:38,188
How do you do, Joe?

1094
01:30:38,438 --> 01:30:40,482
Find the room comfortable, do you?

1095
01:30:40,732 --> 01:30:42,692
No complaints?

1096
01:30:45,779 --> 01:30:47,614
I've heard about you.

1097
01:30:48,698 --> 01:30:50,450
I know what you've done.

1098
01:30:54,788 --> 01:30:58,458
Breaking the hearts of your
poor, grieving parents.

1099
01:30:59,459 --> 01:31:01,211
So you're back, eh?

1100
01:31:01,461 --> 01:31:06,091
Back to make life a misery for
your lovely parents once more?

1101
01:31:06,383 --> 01:31:07,884
Over my dead corpse, you will.

1102
01:31:08,134 --> 01:31:11,429
Because, you see, they've let me
be more like a son to them...

1103
01:31:11,680 --> 01:31:13,640
...than like a lodger.

1104
01:31:15,266 --> 01:31:17,811
Don't go fighting here, boys.

1105
01:31:23,692 --> 01:31:25,527
Do put your hand
over your mouth, please.

1106
01:31:25,819 --> 01:31:27,028
It's bloody revolting.

1107
01:31:32,575 --> 01:31:34,160
Are you all right?

1108
01:31:35,328 --> 01:31:36,996
It's the treatment.

1109
01:31:37,247 --> 01:31:39,874
It's disgusting.
Enough to put you off your food.

1110
01:31:40,125 --> 01:31:43,920
Leave him be, Joe.
It's the treatment.

1111
01:31:46,006 --> 01:31:48,800
Do you think we ought
to do something?

1112
01:31:49,884 --> 01:31:53,221
Would you like me to make you
a nice cup of tea, son?

1113
01:32:03,982 --> 01:32:07,068
What have you done
with all me own personal things?

1114
01:32:11,364 --> 01:32:14,117
That was all...

1115
01:32:14,367 --> 01:32:16,036
...took away, son.

1116
01:32:16,619 --> 01:32:18,413
By the police.

1117
01:32:18,830 --> 01:32:20,749
New regulation, see...

1118
01:32:20,999 --> 01:32:24,044
...about compensation
for the victims.

1119
01:32:26,755 --> 01:32:28,381
What about Basil?

1120
01:32:31,384 --> 01:32:33,136
Where is my snake?

1121
01:32:43,396 --> 01:32:44,606
He met with...

1122
01:32:44,856 --> 01:32:46,649
...like, an accident.

1123
01:32:50,612 --> 01:32:52,072
He passed away.

1124
01:32:57,410 --> 01:32:59,537
What's going to happen to me, then?

1125
01:33:01,790 --> 01:33:02,999
I mean...

1126
01:33:04,125 --> 01:33:05,585
...that's my room he's in.

1127
01:33:05,835 --> 01:33:07,712
There's no denying that.

1128
01:33:08,755 --> 01:33:11,341
This is my home also.

1129
01:33:13,259 --> 01:33:16,721
What suggestions have you,
my Pee and Em, to make?

1130
01:33:22,644 --> 01:33:25,230
All this needs thinking about, son.

1131
01:33:26,481 --> 01:33:29,317
We can't very well
just kick Joe out.

1132
01:33:29,567 --> 01:33:31,403
Not just like that, can we?

1133
01:33:31,653 --> 01:33:32,696
I mean...

1134
01:33:32,946 --> 01:33:34,906
...Joe's here doing a job.

1135
01:33:35,156 --> 01:33:37,450
A contract it is.
Two years.

1136
01:33:37,701 --> 01:33:41,413
We made, like, an arrangement.
Didn't we, Joe?

1137
01:33:43,164 --> 01:33:45,125
You see, son...

1138
01:33:46,459 --> 01:33:50,005
...Joe's paid next month's
rent already...

1139
01:33:51,548 --> 01:33:54,384
...so whatever we may do in
the future, we can't just say...

1140
01:33:54,634 --> 01:33:57,637
...to Joe to get out, now can we?

1141
01:33:58,054 --> 01:33:59,931
No, but it's much more than that.

1142
01:34:00,807 --> 01:34:03,226
I mean, I've got you two
to think of...

1143
01:34:03,476 --> 01:34:06,354
...who've been like
a father and mother to me.

1144
01:34:06,604 --> 01:34:09,566
It wouldn't be right for me
to go off and leave you two...

1145
01:34:09,816 --> 01:34:12,736
...to the tender mercies
of this young monster...

1146
01:34:12,986 --> 01:34:16,239
...who's been like
no real son at all.

1147
01:34:16,865 --> 01:34:19,200
Look, he's weeping now.

1148
01:34:19,451 --> 01:34:22,412
But that's all his craft
and artfulness.

1149
01:34:22,746 --> 01:34:25,498
Let him go and find
a room somewhere else.

1150
01:34:25,749 --> 01:34:30,045
Let him learn the errors
of his way, and that a bad boy...

1151
01:34:30,295 --> 01:34:33,757
...doesn't deserve such a good
mum and dad as he's had.

1152
01:34:39,471 --> 01:34:40,764
All right.

1153
01:34:41,848 --> 01:34:43,725
I know how things are now.

1154
01:34:45,185 --> 01:34:47,812
I've suffered and I've suffered...

1155
01:34:48,063 --> 01:34:50,023
...and I've suffered.

1156
01:34:50,732 --> 01:34:53,943
And everybody wants me
to go on suffering.

1157
01:34:55,904 --> 01:34:58,073
You've made others suffer.

1158
01:34:58,573 --> 01:35:01,701
It's only right
that you should suffer proper.

1159
01:35:02,660 --> 01:35:04,329
I've been told
everything you've done...

1160
01:35:04,579 --> 01:35:06,539
...sitting around the family table.

1161
01:35:06,790 --> 01:35:09,876
And pretty shocking
it was to listen to.

1162
01:35:10,794 --> 01:35:13,963
It made me real sick,
a lot of it did.

1163
01:35:15,924 --> 01:35:19,511
Now look what you've gone
and done to your mother.

1164
01:35:19,761 --> 01:35:21,388
Come on. It's all right now.

1165
01:35:34,317 --> 01:35:35,485
Right!

1166
01:35:36,236 --> 01:35:37,946
I'm leaving now.

1167
01:35:38,196 --> 01:35:40,323
You won't ever viddy me no more.

1168
01:35:40,573 --> 01:35:42,283
I'll make me own way.

1169
01:35:42,742 --> 01:35:46,413
Thank you very much. Let it lie
heavy on your consciences.

1170
01:35:47,747 --> 01:35:50,709
Now don't take it like that, son.

1171
01:36:52,979 --> 01:36:55,940
Can you spare some cutter,
me brother?

1172
01:36:57,734 --> 01:37:00,862
Can you spare some cutter,
me brother?

1173
01:37:04,532 --> 01:37:07,619
Can you spare some cutter,
me brother?

1174
01:37:28,932 --> 01:37:30,392
Thanks, brother.

1175
01:37:48,326 --> 01:37:50,161
Jamey Mack!

1176
01:37:50,620 --> 01:37:52,080
May the hokey fly!

1177
01:37:52,414 --> 01:37:55,959
Mother of God and all the blessed
saints in heaven preserve us!

1178
01:37:57,669 --> 01:37:59,754
I never forget a face, me God!

1179
01:38:00,005 --> 01:38:01,339
I never forget any face.

1180
01:38:01,589 --> 01:38:04,384
Leave me alone, brother.
I've never seen you before!

1181
01:38:04,634 --> 01:38:08,096
This is the poisonous young swine
that near done me in.

1182
01:38:08,346 --> 01:38:09,514
Him and his friends.

1183
01:38:09,764 --> 01:38:12,642
They beat me and kicked me
and punched me.

1184
01:38:12,892 --> 01:38:14,436
Stop him! Stop him!

1185
01:38:14,686 --> 01:38:18,606
They laughed at me blood
and me moans, this murderous dog!

1186
01:38:18,857 --> 01:38:22,235
Then there was like
a sea of dirty, smelly old men...

1187
01:38:22,485 --> 01:38:24,571
...trying to get at
your humble narrator...

1188
01:38:24,821 --> 01:38:28,491
... with their feeble rookers
and horny old claws.

1189
01:38:28,742 --> 01:38:31,536
It was old age
having a go at youth.

1190
01:38:32,245 --> 01:38:35,498
And I daren't do a single
solitary thing, O my brothers.

1191
01:38:35,790 --> 01:38:37,792
It being better
to be hit at like that...

1192
01:38:38,043 --> 01:38:40,628
...than want to sick
and feel that horrible pain.

1193
01:38:40,879 --> 01:38:42,297
All right, all right!

1194
01:38:42,547 --> 01:38:43,423
Stop it now!

1195
01:38:43,673 --> 01:38:47,052
Come on. Stop breaking the
state's peace, you naughty boys!

1196
01:38:47,302 --> 01:38:50,138
Back away! Go away with you!

1197
01:38:50,388 --> 01:38:52,682
What's your trouble, sir?

1198
01:39:00,315 --> 01:39:01,691
Well!

1199
01:39:02,359 --> 01:39:04,819
Well, well, well!

1200
01:39:08,740 --> 01:39:11,242
If it isn't little Alex.

1201
01:39:11,493 --> 01:39:12,869
Long time no viddy, droog.

1202
01:39:13,119 --> 01:39:14,579
How goes?

1203
01:39:14,829 --> 01:39:16,081
It's impossible.

1204
01:39:16,331 --> 01:39:17,540
I don't believe it.

1205
01:39:17,791 --> 01:39:19,668
Evidence of the old glazzies.

1206
01:39:19,918 --> 01:39:21,711
Nothing up our sleeves.

1207
01:39:21,961 --> 01:39:24,005
No magic, little Alex.

1208
01:39:24,255 --> 01:39:27,717
A job for two
who are now of job age.

1209
01:39:28,093 --> 01:39:29,511
The police.

1210
01:39:45,235 --> 01:39:46,444
Come on, Alex.

1211
01:39:46,695 --> 01:39:48,238
Come for walking.

1212
01:39:59,833 --> 01:40:02,252
Come, come, come,
my little droogies.

1213
01:40:02,502 --> 01:40:04,045
I just don't get this at all.

1214
01:40:04,295 --> 01:40:06,464
The old days are dead and gone.

1215
01:40:06,715 --> 01:40:09,551
For what I did in the past,
I've been punished.

1216
01:40:09,843 --> 01:40:11,511
I've been cured.

1217
01:40:11,761 --> 01:40:12,971
That was read out to us.

1218
01:40:13,221 --> 01:40:15,056
The inspector read it
all out to us.

1219
01:40:15,306 --> 01:40:17,976
He said it was a very good way.

1220
01:40:18,226 --> 01:40:19,477
But what is all this?

1221
01:40:19,769 --> 01:40:22,272
It was them
that went for me, brothers.

1222
01:40:22,522 --> 01:40:25,191
You're not on their side,
and can't be.

1223
01:40:25,775 --> 01:40:27,944
You can't be, Dim.

1224
01:40:28,194 --> 01:40:30,864
It was someone we fillied with
back in the old days...

1225
01:40:31,114 --> 01:40:34,576
...trying to get his own revenge
after all this time. Remember?

1226
01:40:34,826 --> 01:40:36,244
A long time is right.

1227
01:40:36,494 --> 01:40:38,747
I don't remember them days
too horrorshow.

1228
01:40:38,997 --> 01:40:41,082
And don't call me Dim
no more, either.

1229
01:40:41,332 --> 01:40:43,418
Officer, call me.

1230
01:40:43,752 --> 01:40:47,213
Enough is remembered, though,
little Alex.

1231
01:40:47,839 --> 01:40:50,925
And this is to make sure
you stay cured.

1232
01:41:46,856 --> 01:41:47,982
That's enough.

1233
01:41:48,233 --> 01:41:50,860
A bit more. He's still kicking.

1234
01:42:09,713 --> 01:42:11,548
Cured, are you?

1235
01:42:13,216 --> 01:42:17,053
Be viddying you some more
sometime, droogie.

1236
01:42:32,318 --> 01:42:36,322
Where was I to go,
who had no home and no money?

1237
01:42:36,573 --> 01:42:38,783
I cried for meself.

1238
01:42:39,117 --> 01:42:41,911
Home, home, home.

1239
01:42:42,162 --> 01:42:44,039
It was home I was wanting.

1240
01:42:44,289 --> 01:42:47,292
And it was home
I came to, brothers...

1241
01:42:47,542 --> 01:42:50,170
...not realizing,
in the state I was in...

1242
01:42:50,420 --> 01:42:53,423
... where I was
and had been before.

1243
01:43:41,638 --> 01:43:43,640
Who on earth could that be?

1244
01:43:59,197 --> 01:44:00,865
I'll see who it is.

1245
01:44:12,419 --> 01:44:14,004
Yes, what is it?

1246
01:44:22,679 --> 01:44:23,888
Please...

1247
01:44:40,739 --> 01:44:44,075
Frank, I think this young man
needs some help.

1248
01:44:48,788 --> 01:44:50,206
My God!

1249
01:44:51,166 --> 01:44:53,418
What's happened to you, my boy?

1250
01:44:55,879 --> 01:44:59,549
And would you believe it,
O my brothers and only friends...

1251
01:44:59,799 --> 01:45:02,052
...there was your
faithful narrator...

1252
01:45:02,302 --> 01:45:04,763
...being held helpless
like a babe in arms...

1253
01:45:05,013 --> 01:45:07,390
...and suddenly realizing
where he was...

1254
01:45:07,640 --> 01:45:11,061
...and why "home" on the gate
had looked so familiar.

1255
01:45:11,311 --> 01:45:13,063
But I knew I was safe.

1256
01:45:13,313 --> 01:45:15,357
I knew he would not remember me.

1257
01:45:15,607 --> 01:45:17,359
For in those carefree days...

1258
01:45:17,609 --> 01:45:19,486
...I and my so-called droogs...

1259
01:45:19,736 --> 01:45:23,239
... wore our maskies, which were
like real horrorshow disguises.

1260
01:45:24,532 --> 01:45:25,742
Police.

1261
01:45:29,412 --> 01:45:31,581
Ghastly, horrible police...

1262
01:45:33,583 --> 01:45:35,168
...they beat me up, sir.

1263
01:45:39,464 --> 01:45:41,841
The police beat me up.

1264
01:45:43,927 --> 01:45:45,595
I know you!

1265
01:45:49,808 --> 01:45:51,935
Isn't it your picture
in the newspapers?

1266
01:45:52,185 --> 01:45:54,396
Didn't I see you
on the video this morning?

1267
01:45:54,646 --> 01:45:57,982
Are you not the poor victim
of this horrible new technique?

1268
01:45:58,274 --> 01:45:59,526
Yes, sir.

1269
01:45:59,984 --> 01:46:03,196
That's exactly who I am and
what I am, sir. A victim.

1270
01:46:03,446 --> 01:46:06,574
Then, by God, you've been
sent here by providence!

1271
01:46:06,825 --> 01:46:09,911
Tortured in prison, then
tortured by the police.

1272
01:46:10,161 --> 01:46:14,666
My heart goes out to you.
You're not the first to come here.

1273
01:46:14,916 --> 01:46:17,794
The police like to bring
their victims to this village.

1274
01:46:18,044 --> 01:46:19,421
But it's providential that you...

1275
01:46:19,671 --> 01:46:23,216
...who are also another kind
of victim, should come here.

1276
01:46:25,176 --> 01:46:28,221
But you're cold and shivering.

1277
01:46:28,722 --> 01:46:30,098
Julian...

1278
01:46:30,348 --> 01:46:32,600
...draw a bath for this young man.

1279
01:46:32,851 --> 01:46:34,185
Certainly, Frank.

1280
01:46:34,561 --> 01:46:36,187
Thank you very much.

1281
01:46:36,438 --> 01:46:38,064
God bless you.

1282
01:47:32,994 --> 01:47:35,288
He can be the most potent
weapon imaginable...

1283
01:47:35,538 --> 01:47:38,708
...to ensure the government
is not returned in the election.

1284
01:47:38,958 --> 01:47:40,752
The government's big boast, sir...

1285
01:47:41,002 --> 01:47:43,713
...is the way they have
dealt with crime:

1286
01:47:43,963 --> 01:47:45,799
Recruiting young roughs
into the police...

1287
01:47:46,049 --> 01:47:49,094
...proposing will-sapping
techniques of conditioning.

1288
01:47:49,344 --> 01:47:51,596
We've seen it before
in other countries.

1289
01:47:51,846 --> 01:47:53,306
The thin end of the wedge.

1290
01:47:53,556 --> 01:47:57,644
Before we know it, we'll have the
full apparatus of totalitarianism.

1291
01:48:01,690 --> 01:48:06,069
This young boy is a living witness
to these diabolical proposals.

1292
01:48:06,319 --> 01:48:10,073
The people, the common people,
must know, must see.

1293
01:48:10,323 --> 01:48:14,703
There are traditions of liberty to
defend. That tradition is all.

1294
01:48:14,953 --> 01:48:16,913
The common people
will let it go, yes.

1295
01:48:17,163 --> 01:48:19,290
They'll sell liberty
for a quieter life.

1296
01:48:19,541 --> 01:48:21,084
That is why they must be led.

1297
01:48:21,334 --> 01:48:23,420
Driven. Pushed.

1298
01:48:28,466 --> 01:48:29,718
Fine.

1299
01:48:30,760 --> 01:48:32,429
Thank you very much, sir.

1300
01:48:34,472 --> 01:48:36,016
He'll be here.

1301
01:48:39,227 --> 01:48:42,522
I'm singing in the rain

1302
01:48:43,314 --> 01:48:46,276
Just singing in the rain

1303
01:48:47,110 --> 01:48:50,280
What a glorious feeling

1304
01:48:50,655 --> 01:48:53,992
I'm hap-hap-happy again

1305
01:48:54,617 --> 01:48:57,746
I'm laughing at clouds

1306
01:48:58,538 --> 01:49:01,082
So dark up above

1307
01:49:02,083 --> 01:49:04,544
The sun's in my heart

1308
01:49:05,378 --> 01:49:09,341
I'm ready for love

1309
01:49:10,258 --> 01:49:13,011
Let the stormy clouds chase

1310
01:49:13,636 --> 01:49:16,473
Everyone from the place

1311
01:49:17,932 --> 01:49:22,937
Come on with the rain
I've a smile on my face

1312
01:49:23,563 --> 01:49:26,566
I'll walk down the lane

1313
01:50:00,767 --> 01:50:02,227
Good evening, sir.

1314
01:50:06,189 --> 01:50:07,732
Good evening.

1315
01:50:08,274 --> 01:50:11,111
It was very kind of you
to leave this out for me.

1316
01:50:11,361 --> 01:50:13,780
There was no one around,
so I started.

1317
01:50:14,030 --> 01:50:15,865
Hope that's all right, sir.

1318
01:50:19,369 --> 01:50:21,079
Of course.

1319
01:50:51,943 --> 01:50:54,320
Food all right?

1320
01:51:00,035 --> 01:51:01,745
Great, sir. Great.

1321
01:51:04,706 --> 01:51:06,958
Try the wine.

1322
01:51:13,340 --> 01:51:14,632
Thank you, sir.

1323
01:51:17,302 --> 01:51:18,553
Cheers.

1324
01:51:20,597 --> 01:51:21,806
Happy days.

1325
01:51:32,317 --> 01:51:34,611
Won't you join me?

1326
01:51:35,362 --> 01:51:37,572
My health doesn't allow it.

1327
01:51:38,406 --> 01:51:39,741
No, thank you.

1328
01:51:45,705 --> 01:51:48,166
" 1960, Château...

1329
01:51:48,708 --> 01:51:50,627
...Saint-Estèphe.

1330
01:51:50,877 --> 01:51:51,711
Médoc."

1331
01:51:51,961 --> 01:51:52,921
Very good brand.

1332
01:52:01,638 --> 01:52:02,639
Very good...

1333
01:52:02,889 --> 01:52:04,140
...color, sir.

1334
01:52:08,353 --> 01:52:10,063
Smells nice too.

1335
01:52:24,994 --> 01:52:27,038
Very nice little number.

1336
01:52:28,248 --> 01:52:29,582
Here's to it.

1337
01:52:38,299 --> 01:52:40,844
Very refreshing, sir.
Very refreshing.

1338
01:52:41,094 --> 01:52:44,014
I'm pleased you
appreciate good wine.

1339
01:52:45,140 --> 01:52:47,017
Have another glass.

1340
01:53:00,155 --> 01:53:01,531
My wife...

1341
01:53:02,991 --> 01:53:06,494
...used to do everything for me
and leave me to my writing.

1342
01:53:09,414 --> 01:53:11,082
Your wife? Is she away?

1343
01:53:11,458 --> 01:53:13,793
She's dead!

1344
01:53:17,922 --> 01:53:19,758
I'm sorry to hear about that.

1345
01:53:20,008 --> 01:53:22,385
She was very badly raped, you see.

1346
01:53:22,635 --> 01:53:25,055
We were assaulted by
vicious young hoodlums...

1347
01:53:25,305 --> 01:53:27,640
...in this very room
you're sitting in now.

1348
01:53:27,891 --> 01:53:32,645
I was left a helpless cripple,
but for her the agony was too great.

1349
01:53:32,979 --> 01:53:34,814
The doctors said
it was pneumonia...

1350
01:53:35,065 --> 01:53:37,901
...because it happened later,
during a flu epidemic.

1351
01:53:38,151 --> 01:53:42,405
The doctors told me it was
pneumonia, but I knew what it was.

1352
01:53:42,655 --> 01:53:46,993
A victim of the modern age.
Poor, poor girl!

1353
01:53:50,997 --> 01:53:52,582
And now you.

1354
01:53:53,166 --> 01:53:56,211
Another victim of the modern age.

1355
01:53:56,503 --> 01:53:58,463
But you can be helped.

1356
01:53:59,464 --> 01:54:02,926
I phoned some friends while
you were having your bath.

1357
01:54:03,176 --> 01:54:04,010
Some...

1358
01:54:04,260 --> 01:54:05,345
...friends?

1359
01:54:05,595 --> 01:54:07,138
They want to help you.

1360
01:54:07,389 --> 01:54:09,641
-Help me?
-Help you.

1361
01:54:09,891 --> 01:54:13,395
-Who are they?
-Very, very important people.

1362
01:54:13,645 --> 01:54:16,022
And they're interested in you.

1363
01:54:21,486 --> 01:54:23,655
This'll be these people now.

1364
01:54:23,905 --> 01:54:27,325
I don't want to trouble you
any further. I should be leaving.

1365
01:54:28,410 --> 01:54:30,370
No trouble at all.

1366
01:54:31,079 --> 01:54:32,288
Here.

1367
01:54:32,539 --> 01:54:34,457
Let me fill your glass.

1368
01:55:00,150 --> 01:55:01,901
So this is the young man.

1369
01:55:03,278 --> 01:55:04,738
How do you do, sir?

1370
01:55:05,113 --> 01:55:07,741
Missus.
I'm very pleased to meet you.

1371
01:55:08,116 --> 01:55:10,618
I hope you forgive us for coming
at this hour...

1372
01:55:10,869 --> 01:55:12,746
...but we heard you
were in trouble...

1373
01:55:12,996 --> 01:55:15,248
...and so we came over to see
if we could help.

1374
01:55:15,498 --> 01:55:17,751
Very kind of you, sir.
Thank you very much.

1375
01:55:18,001 --> 01:55:20,253
I understand you had a rather...

1376
01:55:20,503 --> 01:55:21,755
...unfortunate...

1377
01:55:22,005 --> 01:55:23,506
...encounter...

1378
01:55:23,757 --> 01:55:25,508
...with the police tonight.

1379
01:55:25,759 --> 01:55:27,844
Yes, I suppose
you could call it that.

1380
01:55:28,094 --> 01:55:29,429
How are you feeling now?

1381
01:55:29,679 --> 01:55:30,930
Much better, thank you.

1382
01:55:31,181 --> 01:55:33,558
Feel like talking,
answering a few questions?

1383
01:55:33,808 --> 01:55:35,143
Fine, sir. Fine.

1384
01:55:35,977 --> 01:55:38,646
As I said, we've heard about you.

1385
01:55:39,147 --> 01:55:41,775
We are interested in your case.

1386
01:55:42,025 --> 01:55:44,903
-We want to help you.
-Thank you very much.

1387
01:55:45,195 --> 01:55:48,323
Shall we get down to it?

1388
01:55:48,573 --> 01:55:50,367
Fine. Fine, sir.

1389
01:55:55,663 --> 01:55:58,416
The newspapers mentioned...

1390
01:55:58,667 --> 01:56:02,962
...in addition to being conditioned
against acts of sex and violence...

1391
01:56:03,213 --> 01:56:06,591
...you've inadvertently been
conditioned against music.

1392
01:56:07,550 --> 01:56:10,637
I think that was something
that they didn't plan for.

1393
01:56:10,970 --> 01:56:12,889
You see, missus...

1394
01:56:13,139 --> 01:56:16,643
...l'm very fond of music.
Especially Beethoven.

1395
01:56:17,769 --> 01:56:19,729
Ludwig van Beethoven.

1396
01:56:19,979 --> 01:56:22,273
-B-E...
-lt's all right, thank you.

1397
01:56:22,816 --> 01:56:26,903
And it just so happened that
while they were showing me...

1398
01:56:27,153 --> 01:56:31,074
...a particularly bad film
of, like, a concentration camp...

1399
01:56:31,324 --> 01:56:34,869
...the background music
was playing Beethoven.

1400
01:56:35,120 --> 01:56:37,872
So now you have
the same reaction to music...

1401
01:56:38,123 --> 01:56:39,874
...as you do to sex and violence?

1402
01:56:40,125 --> 01:56:44,421
No, missus. You see, it's not
all music. It's just the Ninth.

1403
01:56:44,671 --> 01:56:46,423
You mean Beethoven's Ninth Symphony?

1404
01:56:46,673 --> 01:56:49,718
That's right. I can't listen
to the Ninth anymore at all.

1405
01:56:49,968 --> 01:56:53,430
When I hear the Ninth, I get, like...

1406
01:56:53,680 --> 01:56:55,306
...this funny feeling.

1407
01:56:56,349 --> 01:57:00,645
And then all I can think about
is, like, trying to snuff it.

1408
01:57:00,895 --> 01:57:05,316
-I beg your pardon?
-Snuff it. Death, I mean.

1409
01:57:05,567 --> 01:57:08,153
I just want to die peacefully...

1410
01:57:08,611 --> 01:57:10,947
...like, with no pain.

1411
01:57:11,698 --> 01:57:13,575
Do you feel that way now?

1412
01:57:14,743 --> 01:57:16,703
No, sir, not exactly.

1413
01:57:16,953 --> 01:57:18,204
I still feel...

1414
01:57:18,455 --> 01:57:19,706
...very miserable.

1415
01:57:19,956 --> 01:57:22,500
Very much down in spirits.

1416
01:57:23,001 --> 01:57:24,336
Do you still feel...

1417
01:57:24,586 --> 01:57:26,087
...suicidal?

1418
01:57:29,341 --> 01:57:31,092
Put it this way:

1419
01:57:31,384 --> 01:57:34,220
I feel very low in myself.

1420
01:57:35,055 --> 01:57:37,390
I can't see much in the future.

1421
01:57:37,640 --> 01:57:42,103
I feel that any second, something
terrible is going to happen to me.

1422
01:57:55,325 --> 01:57:56,993
Well done, Frank.

1423
01:58:03,041 --> 01:58:04,834
Get the car, would you, please?

1424
01:58:25,438 --> 01:58:26,815
I woke up...

1425
01:58:32,362 --> 01:58:36,116
...the pain and sickness
all over me like an animal.

1426
01:58:44,165 --> 01:58:47,002
Then I realized what it was.

1427
01:58:48,294 --> 01:58:51,089
The music coming up
from the floor...

1428
01:58:51,339 --> 01:58:54,509
... was our old friend,
Ludwig van...

1429
01:58:54,759 --> 01:58:57,429
...and the dreaded Ninth Symphony.

1430
01:59:05,353 --> 01:59:06,730
Let me out!

1431
01:59:06,980 --> 01:59:08,732
Open the door!

1432
01:59:09,441 --> 01:59:11,609
Come on, open the door!

1433
01:59:14,154 --> 01:59:15,447
Turn it off!

1434
01:59:15,697 --> 01:59:17,449
Turn it off!

1435
01:59:24,372 --> 01:59:25,290
Stop it!

1436
02:00:13,546 --> 02:00:15,090
Turn it off!

1437
02:00:16,508 --> 02:00:17,467
Please!

1438
02:00:17,717 --> 02:00:19,886
Turn it off!

1439
02:00:33,817 --> 02:00:36,695
Suddenly, I viddied
what I had to do...

1440
02:00:36,945 --> 02:00:39,280
...and what I had wanted to do.

1441
02:00:39,698 --> 02:00:42,117
And that was to do myself in.

1442
02:00:42,534 --> 02:00:43,910
To snuff it.

1443
02:00:44,244 --> 02:00:47,622
To blast off forever,
out of this wicked, cruel world.

1444
02:00:49,207 --> 02:00:51,626
One moment of pain, perhaps...

1445
02:00:51,918 --> 02:00:53,712
...and then sleep.

1446
02:00:53,962 --> 02:00:56,464
Forever and ever...

1447
02:00:56,715 --> 02:00:58,049
...and ever.

1448
02:01:22,490 --> 02:01:24,284
I jumped, O my brothers...

1449
02:01:24,534 --> 02:01:25,994
...and I fell hard.

1450
02:01:26,244 --> 02:01:28,538
But I did not snuff it.

1451
02:01:29,164 --> 02:01:30,749
If I had snuffed it...

1452
02:01:30,999 --> 02:01:34,294
...I would not be here
to tell what I told have.

1453
02:01:36,212 --> 02:01:40,842
I came back to life
after a long, black, black gap...

1454
02:01:41,092 --> 02:01:44,387
...of what might have been
a million years.

1455
02:02:13,124 --> 02:02:15,669
He's recovered
consciousness, Doctor.

1456
02:02:55,750 --> 02:02:57,252
Hello, lad.

1457
02:02:57,502 --> 02:02:59,087
Hello, son.

1458
02:03:00,046 --> 02:03:01,506
How are you?

1459
02:03:02,632 --> 02:03:04,634
You feeling better?

1460
02:03:09,097 --> 02:03:10,140
What...

1461
02:03:10,390 --> 02:03:11,433
...gives...

1462
02:03:12,892 --> 02:03:14,894
...O my Pee and Em?

1463
02:03:15,895 --> 02:03:17,439
What makes...

1464
02:03:18,231 --> 02:03:19,149
...you think...

1465
02:03:19,399 --> 02:03:21,860
...you are welcome?

1466
02:03:24,779 --> 02:03:26,740
There, there, Mother.
It's all right.

1467
02:03:26,990 --> 02:03:28,616
He doesn't mean it.

1468
02:03:31,077 --> 02:03:33,621
You were in the papers again, son.

1469
02:03:34,414 --> 02:03:35,957
It said...

1470
02:03:36,207 --> 02:03:38,960
...they had done
great wrong to you.

1471
02:03:39,836 --> 02:03:41,171
It said...

1472
02:03:41,421 --> 02:03:42,756
...how the government...

1473
02:03:43,006 --> 02:03:45,008
...drove you to try...

1474
02:03:45,258 --> 02:03:46,843
...and do yourself in.

1475
02:03:48,636 --> 02:03:50,930
And when you think about it, son...

1476
02:03:52,015 --> 02:03:54,642
...maybe it was our fault too...

1477
02:03:55,018 --> 02:03:56,269
...in a way.

1478
02:03:57,395 --> 02:03:59,314
Your home's your home...

1479
02:03:59,647 --> 02:04:02,150
...when all's said and done, son.

1480
02:04:12,160 --> 02:04:14,662
-Good morning.
-Good morning, Doctor.

1481
02:04:23,630 --> 02:04:25,882
-How are you feeling today?
-Fine.

1482
02:04:26,132 --> 02:04:27,258
Good. May I?

1483
02:04:27,676 --> 02:04:29,719
-I'm Dr. Taylor.
-Haven't seen you before.

1484
02:04:29,969 --> 02:04:31,262
I'm your psychiatrist.

1485
02:04:31,513 --> 02:04:33,390
Psychiatrist!
Do I need one?

1486
02:04:33,640 --> 02:04:35,141
Just part of hospital routine.

1487
02:04:35,350 --> 02:04:37,519
Are we going to
talk about me sex life?

1488
02:04:39,229 --> 02:04:41,231
I'm going to show you
some slides...

1489
02:04:41,481 --> 02:04:44,317
...and you're going to tell me
what you think about them.

1490
02:04:45,235 --> 02:04:46,111
Jolly good.

1491
02:04:48,238 --> 02:04:49,823
You know anything about dreams?

1492
02:04:50,240 --> 02:04:51,366
Something, yes.

1493
02:04:51,616 --> 02:04:53,368
-You know what they mean?
-Perhaps.

1494
02:04:53,576 --> 02:04:55,036
You concerned about something?

1495
02:04:55,286 --> 02:04:58,289
No, not concerned, really...

1496
02:04:58,540 --> 02:05:00,542
...but I've been having
this nasty dream.

1497
02:05:00,792 --> 02:05:02,252
Very nasty.

1498
02:05:02,502 --> 02:05:04,421
It's like...

1499
02:05:06,423 --> 02:05:08,591
...when I was all smashed up,
you know...

1500
02:05:08,842 --> 02:05:10,885
...and half-awake
and unconscious-like...

1501
02:05:11,136 --> 02:05:13,263
...I kept having this dream.

1502
02:05:13,513 --> 02:05:16,391
All these doctors were
playing around with me gulliver.

1503
02:05:16,641 --> 02:05:18,727
You know, like the inside
of me brain.

1504
02:05:18,977 --> 02:05:21,855
I seem to have this dream
over and over again.

1505
02:05:22,105 --> 02:05:24,232
Do you think it means anything?

1506
02:05:25,150 --> 02:05:29,571
Patients with injuries like yours
often have dreams of this sort.

1507
02:05:29,821 --> 02:05:31,906
It's all part
of the recovery process.

1508
02:05:33,158 --> 02:05:35,952
Now then, each of these slides
needs a reply...

1509
02:05:36,202 --> 02:05:38,204
...from one of the people
in the picture.

1510
02:05:38,455 --> 02:05:41,666
You tell me what you think
the person would say...

1511
02:05:41,916 --> 02:05:42,792
...all right?

1512
02:05:43,043 --> 02:05:44,461
Righty-right.

1513
02:05:46,463 --> 02:05:48,840
"Isn't the plumage beautiful?"

1514
02:05:50,091 --> 02:05:52,552
I just say what the
other person would say?

1515
02:05:56,723 --> 02:05:58,266
Don't think about it too long.

1516
02:05:58,516 --> 02:06:01,019
Say the first thing
that pops into your mind.

1517
02:06:03,688 --> 02:06:06,066
Cabbages. Knickers.

1518
02:06:07,233 --> 02:06:09,527
It's not got a beak.

1519
02:06:09,778 --> 02:06:11,071
Good.

1520
02:06:14,741 --> 02:06:18,661
"The boy you always quarreled with
is seriously ill."

1521
02:06:19,621 --> 02:06:21,373
My mind is a blank...

1522
02:06:22,415 --> 02:06:26,336
...and I'll smash your face
for you, yarblockos.

1523
02:06:26,586 --> 02:06:27,587
Good.

1524
02:06:30,173 --> 02:06:32,258
"What do you want?"

1525
02:06:33,385 --> 02:06:36,763
No time for the old in-out, love.
I've just come to read the meter.

1526
02:06:37,138 --> 02:06:38,515
Good.

1527
02:06:41,976 --> 02:06:45,480
"You sold me a crummy watch.
I want my money back."

1528
02:06:45,980 --> 02:06:49,192
You know what you can do with
that watch? Stick it up your ass!

1529
02:06:53,571 --> 02:06:56,282
"You can do whatever
you like with these."

1530
02:06:57,867 --> 02:06:59,619
Eggiwegs.

1531
02:07:00,161 --> 02:07:02,122
I would like...

1532
02:07:02,372 --> 02:07:03,665
...to smash them.

1533
02:07:04,499 --> 02:07:05,750
And pick them all up...

1534
02:07:06,001 --> 02:07:07,627
...and throw...

1535
02:07:07,877 --> 02:07:09,337
Fucking hell!

1536
02:07:10,213 --> 02:07:12,549
There. That's all there is to it.

1537
02:07:13,216 --> 02:07:14,718
Are you all right?

1538
02:07:15,593 --> 02:07:16,928
Hope so.

1539
02:07:17,178 --> 02:07:20,223
Is that the end, then?
I was quite enjoying that.

1540
02:07:20,557 --> 02:07:21,850
Good. I'm glad.

1541
02:07:22,142 --> 02:07:23,268
How many did I get right?

1542
02:07:23,518 --> 02:07:25,311
It's not that kind of a test.

1543
02:07:25,562 --> 02:07:28,898
But you seem well on the way
to making a complete recovery.

1544
02:07:29,524 --> 02:07:30,942
When do I get out, then?

1545
02:07:31,192 --> 02:07:33,778
I'm sure it won't be long now.

1546
02:07:35,196 --> 02:07:36,781
So I waited...

1547
02:07:37,032 --> 02:07:38,533
...and, O my brothers...

1548
02:07:38,908 --> 02:07:40,326
...I got a lot better...

1549
02:07:40,577 --> 02:07:43,830
...munching away at eggiwegs
and lomticks of toast...

1550
02:07:44,080 --> 02:07:46,499
...and lovely steakie-wakes.

1551
02:07:46,750 --> 02:07:48,209
And then one day...

1552
02:07:48,460 --> 02:07:52,630
...they said I was going to have
a very special visitor.

1553
02:07:58,053 --> 02:08:00,764
Just wait outside for a moment,
would you, Officer?

1554
02:08:03,850 --> 02:08:06,019
I'm afraid my change of schedule
has thrown you.

1555
02:08:06,269 --> 02:08:08,521
The patient's in the middle
of supper.

1556
02:08:08,772 --> 02:08:11,608
That's quite all right, Minister.
No trouble at all.

1557
02:08:13,068 --> 02:08:16,071
-Good evening, my boy.
-Hi there, my little droogies.

1558
02:08:16,321 --> 02:08:18,114
How are you getting on, young man?

1559
02:08:18,490 --> 02:08:20,700
Great, sir. Just great.

1560
02:08:21,493 --> 02:08:23,036
Can I do anything more for you?

1561
02:08:23,286 --> 02:08:25,038
I don't think so, Sir Leslie.

1562
02:08:25,288 --> 02:08:27,957
Then I leave you to it.
Nurse!

1563
02:08:30,794 --> 02:08:34,047
You seem to have a whole ward
to yourself, my boy.

1564
02:08:34,297 --> 02:08:35,590
Yes, sir.

1565
02:08:36,132 --> 02:08:38,468
And a very lonely place
it is too...

1566
02:08:38,718 --> 02:08:41,096
...when I wake up in the night
with me pain.

1567
02:08:42,555 --> 02:08:44,808
Anyway, good to see you
on the mend.

1568
02:08:45,058 --> 02:08:47,644
I kept in touch
with the hospital, of course.

1569
02:08:47,894 --> 02:08:49,729
And now I've come down
personally...

1570
02:08:49,979 --> 02:08:51,564
...to see how you're getting along.

1571
02:08:52,023 --> 02:08:54,275
I've suffered the tortures
of the damned.

1572
02:08:54,526 --> 02:08:56,027
Tortures of the damned.

1573
02:08:56,277 --> 02:08:59,364
Yes, I can appreciate that
you've had an extremely...

1574
02:08:59,614 --> 02:09:02,325
Oh, look. Let me help you
with that, shall I?

1575
02:09:04,536 --> 02:09:08,790
I can tell you that l, and the
government of which I'm a member...

1576
02:09:09,040 --> 02:09:12,961
...are deeply sorry about this,
my boy. Deeply sorry.

1577
02:09:13,211 --> 02:09:14,462
We tried to help you.

1578
02:09:14,713 --> 02:09:18,800
We followed recommendations
that turned out to be wrong.

1579
02:09:19,175 --> 02:09:23,054
An inquiry will place the
responsibility where it belongs.

1580
02:09:23,722 --> 02:09:26,933
We want you to regard us
as friends.

1581
02:09:27,183 --> 02:09:28,393
We put you right.

1582
02:09:28,852 --> 02:09:30,729
You're getting
the best of treatment.

1583
02:09:30,979 --> 02:09:33,231
We never wished you harm.

1584
02:09:33,523 --> 02:09:36,192
But there are some who did, and do.

1585
02:09:36,693 --> 02:09:39,362
And I think you know who those are.

1586
02:09:39,946 --> 02:09:43,742
There are certain people who wanted
to use you for political ends.

1587
02:09:43,992 --> 02:09:46,327
They would have been
glad to have you dead...

1588
02:09:46,578 --> 02:09:49,748
...for they thought they could then
blame it on the government.

1589
02:09:50,331 --> 02:09:52,667
There is also a certain man...

1590
02:09:52,917 --> 02:09:55,420
...a writer of subversive
literature...

1591
02:09:55,670 --> 02:09:57,756
...who has been howling
for your blood.

1592
02:09:58,006 --> 02:10:01,426
He's been mad with desire
to stick a knife into you.

1593
02:10:01,843 --> 02:10:03,386
But you're safe from him now.

1594
02:10:03,636 --> 02:10:05,680
We put him away.

1595
02:10:07,599 --> 02:10:10,685
He found out that you
had done wrong to him.

1596
02:10:11,227 --> 02:10:13,688
At least he believed
you had done wrong.

1597
02:10:13,938 --> 02:10:18,151
He formed this idea in his head
that you had been responsible...

1598
02:10:18,401 --> 02:10:21,821
...for the death of someone
near and dear to him.

1599
02:10:22,697 --> 02:10:23,782
He was a menace.

1600
02:10:24,032 --> 02:10:26,159
We put him away
for his own protection.

1601
02:10:26,368 --> 02:10:27,702
And also for yours.

1602
02:10:28,495 --> 02:10:29,871
Where is he now?

1603
02:10:30,121 --> 02:10:33,583
We put him away
where he can do you no harm.

1604
02:10:33,833 --> 02:10:36,920
You see, we are looking
after your interests.

1605
02:10:37,170 --> 02:10:39,255
We are interested in you.

1606
02:10:39,964 --> 02:10:43,009
When you leave, you'll have no
worries. We'll see to everything.

1607
02:10:43,259 --> 02:10:45,387
A good job on a good salary.

1608
02:10:45,637 --> 02:10:47,347
What job and how much?

1609
02:10:48,223 --> 02:10:52,185
You'll have an interesting job at
a salary you regard as adequate.

1610
02:10:52,435 --> 02:10:54,646
Not only for the job
you're going to do...

1611
02:10:54,896 --> 02:10:58,525
...and in compensation for what
you believe you have suffered...

1612
02:10:58,775 --> 02:11:02,404
...but also because
you are helping us.

1613
02:11:03,697 --> 02:11:05,240
Helping you?

1614
02:11:05,490 --> 02:11:08,618
We always help our friends,
don't we?

1615
02:11:15,166 --> 02:11:17,377
It is no secret
that this government...

1616
02:11:17,627 --> 02:11:20,797
...has lost a lot of popularity
because of you, my boy.

1617
02:11:21,047 --> 02:11:24,426
There are some who think that at
the next election we shall be out.

1618
02:11:24,676 --> 02:11:27,387
The press has chosen to take
a very unfavorable view...

1619
02:11:27,637 --> 02:11:29,055
...of what we tried to do.

1620
02:11:30,015 --> 02:11:33,309
But public opinion
has a way of changing.

1621
02:11:33,560 --> 02:11:35,270
And you, Alex...

1622
02:11:35,520 --> 02:11:37,355
...if I may call you Alex...

1623
02:11:37,605 --> 02:11:40,900
Certainly.
What do they call you at home?

1624
02:11:42,235 --> 02:11:43,528
My name is Frederick.

1625
02:11:44,487 --> 02:11:46,322
As I was saying, Alex...

1626
02:11:46,573 --> 02:11:51,453
...you can be instrumental
in changing the public's verdict.

1627
02:11:54,789 --> 02:11:56,791
Do you understand, Alex?

1628
02:11:57,709 --> 02:11:59,919
Do I make myself clear?

1629
02:12:02,881 --> 02:12:05,175
As an unmuddied lake, Fred.

1630
02:12:05,717 --> 02:12:09,095
As clear as an azure sky
of deepest summer.

1631
02:12:09,346 --> 02:12:10,764
You can rely on me, Fred.

1632
02:12:11,014 --> 02:12:12,349
Good.

1633
02:12:12,599 --> 02:12:14,059
Good boy.

1634
02:12:15,101 --> 02:12:16,936
I understand you're fond of music.

1635
02:12:17,187 --> 02:12:19,397
I have arranged a little
surprise for you.

1636
02:12:19,689 --> 02:12:21,107
Surprise?

1637
02:12:21,358 --> 02:12:23,068
One that I hope
that you will like...

1638
02:12:23,318 --> 02:12:24,694
...as a...

1639
02:12:25,528 --> 02:12:26,905
...how shall we put it...

1640
02:12:27,155 --> 02:12:30,367
...as a symbol of
our new understanding.

1641
02:12:31,368 --> 02:12:34,662
An understanding
between two friends.

1642
02:13:54,701 --> 02:13:57,328
I was cured, all right!
